1
00:00:17,977 --> 00:00:20,395
(MUSIC PLAYING)

2
00:01:13,866 --> 00:01:15,408
(PANTING)

3
00:01:19,038 --> 00:01:20,664
(BEEPING)

4
00:01:30,508 --> 00:01:31,841
- Mama!
- LYRA: We know.

5
00:01:32,009 --> 00:01:34,177
Jyn, gather your things. It's time.

6
00:01:45,481 --> 00:01:47,816
<i>- SAW: Hello?
- Saw, it's Lyra.</i>

7
00:01:48,693 --> 00:01:51,528
It's happened. He's come for us.

8
00:01:51,696 --> 00:01:53,279
<i>You know what to do.</i>

9
00:01:53,531 --> 00:01:55,281
(LOUD HUMMING)

10
00:02:10,423 --> 00:02:11,881
GALEN: Jyn, come here.

11
00:02:12,425 --> 00:02:14,843
Remember, whatever I do,

12
00:02:15,010 --> 00:02:17,011
I do it to protect you.

13
00:02:17,179 --> 00:02:18,847
Say you understand.

14
00:02:19,473 --> 00:02:21,307
I understand.

15
00:02:25,396 --> 00:02:26,396
I love you, Stardust.

16
00:02:27,022 --> 00:02:29,023
I love you, too, Papa.

17
00:02:29,191 --> 00:02:30,483
Galen.

18
00:02:33,237 --> 00:02:34,487
Go.

19
00:02:54,216 --> 00:02:55,717
Jyn.

20
00:02:58,846 --> 00:02:59,846
You know where to go, don't you?

21
00:03:05,227 --> 00:03:06,269
Trust the Force.

22
00:03:08,981 --> 00:03:10,023
(SIGHS)

23
00:03:24,789 --> 00:03:26,581
(PANTING)

24
00:03:39,428 --> 00:03:41,721
You're a hard man to find, Galen.

25
00:03:41,847 --> 00:03:44,140
But farming...

26
00:03:44,308 --> 00:03:47,018
Really? Man of your talents?

27
00:03:47,770 --> 00:03:49,604
It's a peaceful life.

28
00:03:50,147 --> 00:03:52,190
It's lonely, I imagine.

29
00:03:55,444 --> 00:03:56,903
Since Lyra died, yes.

30
00:03:57,738 --> 00:03:58,822
Oh.

31
00:04:00,825 --> 00:04:02,075
Oh...

32
00:04:03,494 --> 00:04:04,786
(EXHALES)

33
00:04:08,040 --> 00:04:10,166
My condolences.

34
00:04:11,502 --> 00:04:13,378
Search the house.

35
00:04:13,712 --> 00:04:15,463
(MECHANICAL VOICES
SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY)

36
00:04:21,720 --> 00:04:23,304
GALEN: What is it you want?

37
00:04:23,472 --> 00:04:26,474
The work has stalled.
I need you to come back.

38
00:04:27,476 --> 00:04:29,018
I won't do it, Krennic.

39
00:04:29,144 --> 00:04:30,645
We were on the verge of greatness.

40
00:04:30,729 --> 00:04:32,397
We were this close

41
00:04:32,565 --> 00:04:35,775
to providing peace
and security for the galaxy.

42
00:04:36,318 --> 00:04:38,111
You're confusing peace with terror.

43
00:04:38,279 --> 00:04:39,279
Well,

44
00:04:39,822 --> 00:04:41,906
you have to start somewhere.

45
00:04:43,492 --> 00:04:45,535
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

46
00:04:47,872 --> 00:04:49,956
I'd be of no help, Krennic.

47
00:04:51,208 --> 00:04:52,792
My mind just isn't what it was.

48
00:04:52,960 --> 00:04:54,544
I have trouble remembering.

49
00:04:55,838 --> 00:04:57,005
Even simple things.

50
00:04:58,674 --> 00:04:59,841
Galen...

51
00:05:00,384 --> 00:05:03,469
You're an inspired scientist,
but you're a terrible liar.

52
00:05:04,054 --> 00:05:05,263
Now, I admire the effort.

53
00:05:05,431 --> 00:05:06,848
I really do.

54
00:05:07,474 --> 00:05:09,809
Oh, look, here's Lyra,
back from the dead.

55
00:05:10,561 --> 00:05:11,811
It's a miracle.

56
00:05:13,022 --> 00:05:14,522
(SPEAKS INDISTINCTLY)

57
00:05:15,024 --> 00:05:16,024
Stop!

58
00:05:18,027 --> 00:05:19,527
(WEAPON WHINES)

59
00:05:19,612 --> 00:05:20,862
Oh, Lyra,

60
00:05:21,447 --> 00:05:22,822
troublesome as ever.

61
00:05:22,990 --> 00:05:24,782
You're not taking him.

62
00:05:24,950 --> 00:05:27,035
No, of course I'm not. I'm taking you all.

63
00:05:27,661 --> 00:05:30,413
You'll all come. You, your child.
You'll all live in comfort.

64
00:05:31,165 --> 00:05:32,373
As hostages.

65
00:05:32,541 --> 00:05:35,960
As heroes of the Empire.

66
00:05:36,128 --> 00:05:39,047
Lyra. Put it down.

67
00:05:40,549 --> 00:05:42,675
Think very carefully.

68
00:05:46,764 --> 00:05:47,847
(BREATH TREMBLING)

69
00:05:50,142 --> 00:05:51,851
- You will never win.
- Do it.

70
00:05:52,394 --> 00:05:53,895
- (WEAPONS FIRING)
- (BOTH GROANING)

71
00:05:54,438 --> 00:05:55,897
- (GASPS)
- Lyra!

72
00:05:56,732 --> 00:05:57,649
Lyra!

73
00:06:00,194 --> 00:06:01,277
They have a child!

74
00:06:02,738 --> 00:06:04,238
Find it!

75
00:06:07,785 --> 00:06:09,369
(JYN PANTING)

76
00:06:19,254 --> 00:06:20,421
(DOOR OPENS)

77
00:06:39,441 --> 00:06:41,776
(MECHANICAL VOICES SPEAKING)

78
00:06:47,866 --> 00:06:49,701
(JYN BREATHING HEAVILY)

79
00:07:01,797 --> 00:07:03,464
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

80
00:07:16,186 --> 00:07:17,979
(JYN CONTINUES PANTING)

81
00:07:23,819 --> 00:07:25,486
(FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING)

82
00:07:33,996 --> 00:07:35,163
My child!

83
00:07:36,707 --> 00:07:37,957
Come.

84
00:07:39,543 --> 00:07:41,169
Come.

85
00:07:41,795 --> 00:07:44,672
We have a long ride ahead of us.

86
00:07:46,633 --> 00:07:48,468
(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)

87
00:08:01,857 --> 00:08:03,441
(WATER DRIPPING)

88
00:08:04,526 --> 00:08:05,943
(DOOR OPENS)

89
00:08:11,033 --> 00:08:13,117
(CELL MATE SNORING)

90
00:08:22,711 --> 00:08:24,045
<i>ANNOUNCER ON PA:
Check in security,</i>

91
00:08:24,129 --> 00:08:26,422
<i>cell block 4227.</i>

92
00:08:27,800 --> 00:08:29,592
<i>4227.</i>

93
00:08:30,260 --> 00:08:32,762
(MAN SCREAMING IN PAIN)

94
00:08:56,328 --> 00:08:58,496
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

95
00:09:04,795 --> 00:09:07,338
(SPEAKING ALIEN LANGUAGE)

96
00:09:13,804 --> 00:09:17,932
STORMTROOPER 1: TK-62, XX-25900.

97
00:09:19,685 --> 00:09:21,435
(INDISTINCT CHATTER CONTINUES)

98
00:09:28,485 --> 00:09:30,611
(TIVIK PANTING)

99
00:09:30,904 --> 00:09:32,280
I was about to leave.

100
00:09:32,447 --> 00:09:33,781
I came as fast as I could.

101
00:09:33,949 --> 00:09:35,867
I have to get back on board.
Walk with me.

102
00:09:36,034 --> 00:09:36,909
Back to Jedha?

103
00:09:37,077 --> 00:09:38,119
They'll leave without me.

104
00:09:38,287 --> 00:09:40,163
Easy! You have news from Jedha.

105
00:09:40,330 --> 00:09:41,706
Come on.

106
00:09:43,167 --> 00:09:46,002
An Imperial pilot,
one of the cargo drivers

107
00:09:46,170 --> 00:09:47,378
he defected yesterday.

108
00:09:48,046 --> 00:09:50,173
He's telling people
they're making a weapon.

109
00:09:50,340 --> 00:09:52,133
The kyber crystals,
that's what they're for.

110
00:09:52,301 --> 00:09:53,217
What kind of weapon?

111
00:09:53,385 --> 00:09:55,887
- Look, I have to go.
- What kind of weapon?

112
00:09:56,054 --> 00:09:58,681
A planet killer! That's what he called it!

113
00:09:58,849 --> 00:10:00,766
A planet killer?

114
00:10:00,934 --> 00:10:03,811
Someone named Erso sent him.
Some old friend of Saw's.

115
00:10:03,979 --> 00:10:05,813
Galen Erso? Was it?

116
00:10:05,981 --> 00:10:08,357
I don't know!
They were looking for Saw when we left.

117
00:10:08,525 --> 00:10:10,818
- Who else knows about this?
- I have no idea.

118
00:10:11,403 --> 00:10:13,237
It's all falling apart.

119
00:10:13,947 --> 00:10:14,697
Saw's right.

120
00:10:14,865 --> 00:10:17,116
- There's spies everywhere.
- (INDISTINCT RADIO CHATTER)

121
00:10:17,910 --> 00:10:18,618
STORMTROOPER 1: What's all this?

122
00:10:20,037 --> 00:10:21,662
<i>Come on, let's see some scandocs.</i>

123
00:10:21,830 --> 00:10:24,540
Yeah, of course. Just... My gloves.

124
00:10:26,168 --> 00:10:27,668
(GROANS)

125
00:10:28,212 --> 00:10:29,795
- No!
- (INDISTINCT YELLING)

126
00:10:29,963 --> 00:10:31,714
What have you done?

127
00:10:32,925 --> 00:10:34,675
<i>Troopers down. Section 9.</i>

128
00:10:34,843 --> 00:10:36,052
TIVIK: Are you crazy?

129
00:10:36,678 --> 00:10:39,013
I'll never climb out of here. My arm!

130
00:10:39,181 --> 00:10:40,264
<i>STORMTROOPER 2:
Get out of the way.</i>

131
00:10:40,432 --> 00:10:41,349
<i>Move! Move!</i>

132
00:10:42,643 --> 00:10:45,061
Hey. Calm down. Calm down.

133
00:10:46,021 --> 00:10:47,813
- It will be all right.
- (BREATHING HEAVILY)

134
00:10:47,898 --> 00:10:49,232
(FIRES WEAPON)

135
00:10:52,152 --> 00:10:53,861
(ALARM BLARING IN THE DISTANCE)

136
00:10:59,701 --> 00:11:05,623
(GRUNTING)

137
00:11:28,230 --> 00:11:29,230
(SPEAKING ALIEN LANGUAGE)

138
00:11:34,236 --> 00:11:35,778
Is that him?

139
00:11:35,946 --> 00:11:39,448
He looks kind of different
to how I imagined.

140
00:11:40,158 --> 00:11:43,786
(SPEAKING ALIEN LANGUAGE)

141
00:11:44,037 --> 00:11:47,540
(GASPS) Okay.
So you're Saw Gerrera?

142
00:11:47,708 --> 00:11:48,666
Saw Gerrera?

143
00:11:49,543 --> 00:11:50,543
No?

144
00:11:51,545 --> 00:11:53,087
Okay, we're just wasting time
that we don't have.

145
00:11:53,255 --> 00:11:55,089
I need to speak to Saw Gerrera.
I keep telling them.

146
00:11:55,257 --> 00:11:56,841
Before it's too late.

147
00:11:57,009 --> 00:11:59,927
(SPEAKING ALIEN LANGUAGE)

148
00:12:00,470 --> 00:12:01,554
We're out here in the middle of nowhere.

149
00:12:01,722 --> 00:12:03,389
We need to get to Jedha City.

150
00:12:03,557 --> 00:12:06,809
What part of "urgent message"
do you guys not understand?

151
00:12:06,977 --> 00:12:08,644
(GRUNTING)

152
00:12:08,895 --> 00:12:10,271
We are all on the same side.

153
00:12:10,439 --> 00:12:12,940
If you just see past
the uniform for a minute.

154
00:12:13,066 --> 00:12:22,199
(CONTINUES SPEAKING
INDISTINCTLY)

155
00:12:52,689 --> 00:12:54,315
(VEHICLE STOPS)

156
00:12:54,816 --> 00:12:55,983
What now?

157
00:12:56,818 --> 00:12:59,361
<i>I don't know. Must be another pickup.</i>

158
00:13:00,655 --> 00:13:01,947
<i>I thought we had everybody.</i>

159
00:13:02,032 --> 00:13:03,491
(DOOR LATCH CLICKS)

160
00:13:06,286 --> 00:13:08,162
(STORMTROOPERS GROANING)

161
00:13:09,456 --> 00:13:10,289
All clear, sir.

162
00:13:10,457 --> 00:13:12,291
Hallik! Liana Hallik!

163
00:13:12,459 --> 00:13:13,375
Her.

164
00:13:14,669 --> 00:13:16,337
You wanna get out of here?

165
00:13:17,172 --> 00:13:18,422
Hey! What about me?

166
00:13:18,799 --> 00:13:19,840
(GRUNTING)

167
00:13:22,010 --> 00:13:24,094
Give me the keys! Give me the keys!

168
00:13:24,179 --> 00:13:25,846
(CONTINUES GRUNTING)

169
00:13:28,225 --> 00:13:30,684
(GROANS)

170
00:13:33,021 --> 00:13:34,855
Congratulations. You are being rescued.

171
00:13:36,775 --> 00:13:38,526
Please do not resist.

172
00:13:53,500 --> 00:13:55,543
(REBEL SOLDIERS
SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY)

173
00:13:57,671 --> 00:14:00,673
<i>REBEL ANNOUNCER: LU-28,
report to maintenance level 4.</i>

174
00:14:06,054 --> 00:14:08,722
(INDISTINCT MECHANICAL CHATTER)

175
00:14:12,644 --> 00:14:15,729
You're currently
calling yourself Liana Hallik.

176
00:14:15,814 --> 00:14:16,897
Is that correct?

177
00:14:18,650 --> 00:14:20,734
Possession of unsanctioned weapons.

178
00:14:20,861 --> 00:14:22,862
Forgery of Imperial documents.

179
00:14:23,029 --> 00:14:24,572
Aggravated assault.
Escape from custody.

180
00:14:24,739 --> 00:14:26,198
Resisting arrest.

181
00:14:27,409 --> 00:14:29,326
Imagine if the Imperial authorities
had found out...

182
00:14:29,494 --> 00:14:32,371
who you really were, Jyn Erso.

183
00:14:33,707 --> 00:14:36,333
That is your given name, is it not?

184
00:14:37,168 --> 00:14:39,587
Jyn Erso, daughter of Galen Erso?

185
00:14:40,505 --> 00:14:43,841
A known Imperial collaborator
in weapons development.

186
00:14:47,512 --> 00:14:49,054
What is this?

187
00:14:49,222 --> 00:14:51,056
MON MOTHMA: It's a chance
for you to make a fresh start.

188
00:14:51,224 --> 00:14:53,017
We think you might be able to help us.

189
00:14:54,102 --> 00:14:56,353
This is Captain Cassian Andor,
Rebel Intelligence.

190
00:14:59,065 --> 00:15:01,609
When was the last time
you were in contact with your father?

191
00:15:03,695 --> 00:15:04,904
15 years ago.

192
00:15:05,572 --> 00:15:08,032
Any idea where he's been all that time?

193
00:15:11,328 --> 00:15:12,411
I like to think he's dead.

194
00:15:12,579 --> 00:15:13,954
Makes things easier.

195
00:15:14,122 --> 00:15:17,291
Easier than what? That he's been a tool
of the Imperial war machine?

196
00:15:17,834 --> 00:15:20,169
I've never had the luxury
of political opinions.

197
00:15:20,337 --> 00:15:21,170
Really?

198
00:15:21,796 --> 00:15:24,632
When was your last contact
with Saw Gerrera?

199
00:15:31,389 --> 00:15:32,640
It's been a long time.

200
00:15:34,225 --> 00:15:35,559
But he'll remember you, though.

201
00:15:35,644 --> 00:15:36,644
Wouldn't he?

202
00:15:36,811 --> 00:15:39,939
He might agree to meet you,
if you came as a friend.

203
00:15:40,649 --> 00:15:43,067
We're up against the clock here, girl,
so if there's nothing to talk about,

204
00:15:43,234 --> 00:15:44,568
we'll just put you back
where we found you.

205
00:15:45,820 --> 00:15:47,988
I was a child.
Saw Gerrera saved my life. He raised me.

206
00:15:48,156 --> 00:15:49,156
But I have no idea where he is.

207
00:15:49,282 --> 00:15:50,324
I haven't seen him in years.

208
00:15:50,492 --> 00:15:51,825
CASSIAN: We know how to find him.

209
00:15:51,910 --> 00:15:53,160
That's not our problem.

210
00:15:53,328 --> 00:15:54,411
What we need is someone

211
00:15:54,496 --> 00:15:56,288
who gets us through the door
without being killed.

212
00:15:58,333 --> 00:16:00,167
You're all rebels, aren't you?

213
00:16:00,335 --> 00:16:03,170
MON MOTHMA: Yes,
but Saw Gerrera is an extremist.

214
00:16:03,338 --> 00:16:05,839
He's been fighting on his own
since he broke with the Rebellion.

215
00:16:06,424 --> 00:16:08,592
His militancy has caused the Alliance

216
00:16:08,677 --> 00:16:10,803
a great many problems.

217
00:16:12,639 --> 00:16:14,264
We have no choice now but to try

218
00:16:14,349 --> 00:16:15,766
and mend that broken trust.

219
00:16:16,518 --> 00:16:18,852
What does this have to do
with my father?

220
00:16:24,484 --> 00:16:27,528
There's an Imperial defector
in Jedha. A pilot.

221
00:16:27,696 --> 00:16:29,363
He's been held by Saw Gerrera.

222
00:16:29,531 --> 00:16:32,449
He's claiming the Emperor
is creating a weapon

223
00:16:32,617 --> 00:16:34,702
with the power to destroy entire planets.

224
00:16:37,414 --> 00:16:41,208
The pilot says
he was sent by your father.

225
00:16:43,044 --> 00:16:44,294
MON MOTHMA:
We need to stop this weapon

226
00:16:44,379 --> 00:16:45,546
before it is finished.

227
00:16:46,172 --> 00:16:47,214
Captain Andor's mission

228
00:16:47,298 --> 00:16:48,549
is to authenticate the pilot's story.

229
00:16:48,717 --> 00:16:50,217
And then, if possible, find your father.

230
00:16:50,385 --> 00:16:52,261
It appears he is critical
to the development

231
00:16:52,345 --> 00:16:53,637
of this super weapon.

232
00:16:53,763 --> 00:16:55,764
Given the gravity of the situation

233
00:16:55,849 --> 00:16:57,683
and your history with Saw,

234
00:16:57,851 --> 00:16:59,852
we're hoping that he will
help us locate your father

235
00:17:00,020 --> 00:17:02,646
and return him
to the Senate for testimony.

236
00:17:11,865 --> 00:17:13,073
And if I do it?

237
00:17:13,825 --> 00:17:16,410
We'll make sure you go free.

238
00:17:20,081 --> 00:17:22,082
(REBEL SOLDIERS
SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY)

239
00:17:35,930 --> 00:17:36,930
DRAVEN: Captain Andor.

240
00:17:39,601 --> 00:17:41,602
(INDISTINCT ANNOUNCEMENT
OVER PA)

241
00:17:48,943 --> 00:17:49,985
I'm K-2SO.

242
00:17:52,363 --> 00:17:54,907
I'm a reprogrammed Imperial droid.

243
00:17:55,742 --> 00:17:57,451
I remember you.

244
00:17:57,619 --> 00:17:59,953
I see the Council is
sending you with us to Jedha.

245
00:18:02,457 --> 00:18:03,791
Apparently so.

246
00:18:05,168 --> 00:18:08,128
That is a bad idea. I think so,
and so does Cassian.

247
00:18:12,550 --> 00:18:13,509
What do I know?

248
00:18:14,094 --> 00:18:15,552
My specialty is just

249
00:18:15,970 --> 00:18:17,429
- strategic analysis.
- (KEYBOARD CLACKING)

250
00:18:17,597 --> 00:18:20,099
Galen Erso is vital to
the Empire's weapons program.

251
00:18:20,266 --> 00:18:21,433
Forget what you heard in there.

252
00:18:21,601 --> 00:18:23,352
There will be no extraction.

253
00:18:23,520 --> 00:18:24,686
You find him...

254
00:18:25,313 --> 00:18:26,605
you kill him.

255
00:18:27,899 --> 00:18:29,566
Then and there.

256
00:18:32,987 --> 00:18:34,988
<i>MALE DISPATCHER: (OVER RADIO)
Shuttle number LMTR-20.</i>

257
00:18:35,156 --> 00:18:38,700
<i>Prepare for takeoff while
we check your authorization.</i>

258
00:18:39,327 --> 00:18:40,244
CASSIAN: You met K-2?

259
00:18:40,411 --> 00:18:41,495
Charming.

260
00:18:42,664 --> 00:18:45,791
He tends to say
whatever comes into his circuits.

261
00:18:45,959 --> 00:18:48,127
It's a byproduct of the reprogram.

262
00:18:48,294 --> 00:18:50,796
Why does she get a blaster and I don't?

263
00:18:52,006 --> 00:18:53,841
- What?
- I know how to use it.

264
00:18:54,008 --> 00:18:56,677
That's what I'm afraid of. Give it to me.

265
00:18:59,722 --> 00:19:01,640
We're going to Jedha.

266
00:19:01,808 --> 00:19:03,183
That's a war zone.

267
00:19:03,351 --> 00:19:05,853
That's not the point. Where'd you get it?

268
00:19:06,479 --> 00:19:07,437
I found it.

269
00:19:07,605 --> 00:19:09,523
K-2SO: I find that answer
vague and unconvincing.

270
00:19:12,694 --> 00:19:14,695
Trust goes both ways.

271
00:19:22,537 --> 00:19:24,246
You're letting her keep it?

272
00:19:25,415 --> 00:19:26,915
Would you like to know the probability

273
00:19:27,041 --> 00:19:29,126
of her using it against you?

274
00:19:31,588 --> 00:19:32,921
It's high.

275
00:19:33,089 --> 00:19:34,506
Let's get going.

276
00:19:34,674 --> 00:19:36,091
It's very high.

277
00:19:36,551 --> 00:19:39,887
- (BUTTONS CLICKING)
- (DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING)

278
00:20:16,257 --> 00:20:17,257
SAW: (SHOUTING) Lies!

279
00:20:20,345 --> 00:20:21,678
Deceptions!

280
00:20:25,934 --> 00:20:26,892
Let's see it.

281
00:20:29,604 --> 00:20:33,190
"Bodhi Rook. Cargo pilot. "

282
00:20:33,358 --> 00:20:35,108
- Local boy, huh?
- Uh-huh.

283
00:20:36,736 --> 00:20:39,404
(SPEAKING ALIEN LANGUAGE)

284
00:20:39,614 --> 00:20:41,531
BODHI: (CHUCKLES)
Okay. I can hear you.

285
00:20:41,699 --> 00:20:43,450
He didn't capture me. I came
here myself. I defected.

286
00:20:43,618 --> 00:20:44,493
I defected.

287
00:20:44,661 --> 00:20:46,995
SAW: Every day, more lies.

288
00:20:47,288 --> 00:20:48,372
(GRUNTS)

289
00:20:48,456 --> 00:20:50,958
Lies? Would I risk everything for a lie?

290
00:20:51,042 --> 00:20:52,292
No, we don't have time for this.

291
00:20:52,460 --> 00:20:53,835
I have to speak to Saw Gerrera
before it's too late.

292
00:20:58,967 --> 00:21:00,550
(EXHALES) Okay.

293
00:21:01,135 --> 00:21:02,636
Sorry, you're...

294
00:21:05,682 --> 00:21:06,807
Um...

295
00:21:07,892 --> 00:21:09,977
(STAMMERS) That's for you.

296
00:21:11,521 --> 00:21:12,437
And I gave it to them.

297
00:21:12,605 --> 00:21:14,314
They did not find it!

298
00:21:15,483 --> 00:21:16,692
I gave it to them.

299
00:21:18,987 --> 00:21:20,404
Uh, Galen Erso.

300
00:21:21,698 --> 00:21:23,824
He told me to find you.

301
00:21:26,911 --> 00:21:28,412
(INHALES DEEPLY)

302
00:21:35,003 --> 00:21:37,004
(GRUNTS)

303
00:21:43,094 --> 00:21:44,011
Bor Gullet.

304
00:21:44,345 --> 00:21:46,346
Uh, Bor Gullet?

305
00:21:47,557 --> 00:21:49,391
What? Wait!

306
00:21:49,517 --> 00:21:50,559
(GRUNTING)

307
00:21:50,685 --> 00:21:52,561
Galen Erso sent me!

308
00:21:52,729 --> 00:21:54,604
He told me to find you.

309
00:21:55,023 --> 00:21:57,733
(DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING)

310
00:22:26,012 --> 00:22:27,304
TARKIN: Most unfortunate about

311
00:22:27,388 --> 00:22:29,765
the security breach on Jedha,
Director Krennic.

312
00:22:29,932 --> 00:22:33,518
After so many setbacks
and delays, and now this.

313
00:22:34,937 --> 00:22:36,188
(SIGHS)

314
00:22:38,900 --> 00:22:42,235
We've heard word of rumors
circulating through the city.

315
00:22:42,904 --> 00:22:44,071
Apparently, you've lost

316
00:22:44,197 --> 00:22:46,406
a rather talkative cargo pilot.

317
00:22:46,574 --> 00:22:48,408
If the Senate gets wind of our project,

318
00:22:48,576 --> 00:22:50,702
countless systems
will flock to the Rebellion.

319
00:22:50,870 --> 00:22:53,413
When the battle station is
finished, Governor Tarkin...

320
00:22:53,581 --> 00:22:55,749
the Senate will be of little concern.

321
00:22:56,751 --> 00:22:59,503
When has become now,
Director Krennic.

322
00:22:59,670 --> 00:23:02,255
The Emperor will tolerate
no further delay.

323
00:23:02,423 --> 00:23:05,342
You have made time
an ally of the Rebellion.

324
00:23:07,136 --> 00:23:09,721
I suggest we solve
both problems simultaneously...

325
00:23:09,889 --> 00:23:12,808
with an immediate test of the weapon.

326
00:23:15,770 --> 00:23:17,896
Failure will find you explaining why

327
00:23:17,980 --> 00:23:20,941
to a far less patient audience.

328
00:23:21,776 --> 00:23:24,152
I will not fail.

329
00:23:24,946 --> 00:23:27,114
(THRILLING MUSIC PLAYING)

330
00:24:02,191 --> 00:24:04,651
What's the matter, Jyn?
You look frightened.

331
00:24:08,030 --> 00:24:10,157
I'll always protect you.

332
00:24:15,496 --> 00:24:16,955
Stardust.

333
00:24:17,665 --> 00:24:18,498
Don't ever change.

334
00:24:22,503 --> 00:24:23,712
LYRA: Trust.

335
00:24:26,382 --> 00:24:27,048
<i>Galen.</i>

336
00:24:29,177 --> 00:24:31,219
- (DOOR OPENS)
- (GASPS)

337
00:24:40,188 --> 00:24:41,980
CASSIAN: We're coming into orbit.
You have controls.

338
00:24:55,119 --> 00:24:56,119
That's Jedha.

339
00:24:58,289 --> 00:24:59,372
Or what's left of it.

340
00:25:01,834 --> 00:25:04,377
We find Saw, we find your father.

341
00:25:11,302 --> 00:25:14,554
(DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING)

342
00:25:48,798 --> 00:25:50,257
What's with the Destroyer?

343
00:25:51,217 --> 00:25:54,094
It's because of
your old friend, Saw Gerrera.

344
00:25:54,262 --> 00:25:56,763
He's been attacking
the cargo shipments.

345
00:25:57,390 --> 00:25:58,932
What are they bringing in?

346
00:26:00,935 --> 00:26:03,478
It's what are they taking out.

347
00:26:04,897 --> 00:26:07,524
Kyber crystal. All they can get.

348
00:26:07,692 --> 00:26:09,442
We wondered why
they were stripping the temple.

349
00:26:09,527 --> 00:26:10,568
Now we know.

350
00:26:10,736 --> 00:26:13,154
It's the fuel for the weapon.

351
00:26:13,322 --> 00:26:15,949
The weapon your father's building.

352
00:26:16,117 --> 00:26:19,202
Maybe we should leave
target practice behind.

353
00:26:19,370 --> 00:26:21,121
Are you talking about me?

354
00:26:21,289 --> 00:26:23,999
She's right. We need to blend in.

355
00:26:24,083 --> 00:26:25,333
Stay with the ship.

356
00:26:25,501 --> 00:26:28,461
I can blend in. I'm an Imperial droid.

357
00:26:28,629 --> 00:26:30,797
The city is under Imperial occupation.

358
00:26:30,965 --> 00:26:32,465
Half the people here
wanna reprogram you.

359
00:26:33,050 --> 00:26:35,302
The other half wanna
put a hole in your head.

360
00:26:35,469 --> 00:26:37,804
I'm surprised
you're so concerned with my safety.

361
00:26:37,972 --> 00:26:38,847
I'm not.

362
00:26:39,015 --> 00:26:42,726
I'm just worried they might
miss you and hit me.

363
00:26:47,940 --> 00:26:50,400
Doesn't sound so bad to me.

364
00:27:00,953 --> 00:27:04,372
- (BOR GULLET GRUNTING)
- (BODHI BREATHING HEAVILY)

365
00:27:09,295 --> 00:27:14,549
SAW: Bor Gullet can feel your thoughts.

366
00:27:17,803 --> 00:27:20,972
No lie is safe.

367
00:27:22,558 --> 00:27:23,558
(GASPING, WHIMPERING)

368
00:27:26,228 --> 00:27:30,732
What have you really
brought me, cargo pilot?

369
00:27:33,986 --> 00:27:37,030
Bor Gullet will know the truth.

370
00:27:38,657 --> 00:27:42,243
The unfortunate side effect
is that one tends...

371
00:27:43,204 --> 00:27:44,621
to lose one's mind.

372
00:27:44,789 --> 00:27:46,373
No! (WHIMPERING)

373
00:27:50,836 --> 00:27:53,004
(SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING)

374
00:27:59,261 --> 00:28:02,430
(INDISTINCT CHATTER
IN ALIEN LANGUAGE)

375
00:28:15,945 --> 00:28:17,404
- (JYN GRUNTS)
- Hey.

376
00:28:17,571 --> 00:28:18,405
You just watch yourself.

377
00:28:18,572 --> 00:28:19,531
Wait. No, no.

378
00:28:19,698 --> 00:28:20,573
Sorry, sir.

379
00:28:20,741 --> 00:28:22,409
We don't want any trouble. Sorry.

380
00:28:22,576 --> 00:28:24,536
Come on. Come on.

381
00:28:24,703 --> 00:28:26,621
<i>MALE IMPERIAL OFFICER:
Citizens of Jedha.</i>

382
00:28:26,789 --> 00:28:28,581
<i>You must come forward with information</i>

383
00:28:28,666 --> 00:28:31,793
<i>of the location
of this missing cargo pilot.</i>

384
00:28:33,796 --> 00:28:35,880
<i>A reward of 600 credits
for the information shall be awarded.</i>

385
00:28:35,965 --> 00:28:36,840
CASSIAN: I had a contact.

386
00:28:37,007 --> 00:28:39,008
One of Saw's Rebels.

387
00:28:39,593 --> 00:28:41,219
But he's just gone missing.

388
00:28:41,387 --> 00:28:43,680
His sister will be looking for him.

389
00:28:44,432 --> 00:28:47,308
The temple's been destroyed,
but she'll be there waiting.

390
00:28:47,476 --> 00:28:48,518
We'll give her your name

391
00:28:48,602 --> 00:28:50,812
and hope that gets us
a meeting with Saw.

392
00:28:50,980 --> 00:28:52,021
Hope?

393
00:28:52,731 --> 00:28:55,900
Yeah. Rebellions are built on hope.

394
00:28:56,068 --> 00:28:57,819
<i>STORMTROOPER 3:
Hands where I can see them.</i>

395
00:28:57,987 --> 00:28:58,987
<i>Get over there.</i>

396
00:28:59,155 --> 00:29:01,531
<i>Show me some identification.
Check inside.</i>

397
00:29:01,615 --> 00:29:03,116
(INDISTINCT YELLING)

398
00:29:03,242 --> 00:29:05,076
Is this all because of your pilot?

399
00:29:09,623 --> 00:29:11,541
CHIRRUT: May the Force
of others be with you.

400
00:29:13,586 --> 00:29:14,961
Wait for me.

401
00:29:15,963 --> 00:29:17,881
CHIRRUT: May the Force
of others be with you.

402
00:29:19,258 --> 00:29:21,634
May the Force of others be with you.

403
00:29:21,802 --> 00:29:24,846
Would you trade that necklace
for a glimpse into your future?

404
00:29:27,141 --> 00:29:27,974
Yes.

405
00:29:28,642 --> 00:29:30,143
I'm speaking to you.

406
00:29:37,735 --> 00:29:39,986
I'm Chirrut îmwe.

407
00:29:41,280 --> 00:29:42,989
How did you know
I was wearing a necklace?

408
00:29:43,157 --> 00:29:45,200
For that answer, you must pay.

409
00:29:49,163 --> 00:29:51,372
What do you know
about kyber crystals?

410
00:29:51,540 --> 00:29:53,041
My father, he...

411
00:29:53,667 --> 00:29:56,169
He said they powered
the Jedi's lightsabers.

412
00:29:57,671 --> 00:29:58,880
Jyn.

413
00:29:59,048 --> 00:30:00,298
Come on. Let's go.

414
00:30:03,677 --> 00:30:06,554
The strongest stars
have hearts of kyber.

415
00:30:10,643 --> 00:30:11,392
Let's go.

416
00:30:12,436 --> 00:30:14,562
We're not here to make friends.

417
00:30:16,023 --> 00:30:17,815
(SPEAKING ALIEN LANGUAGE)

418
00:30:18,692 --> 00:30:19,609
Who are they?

419
00:30:19,777 --> 00:30:21,528
The Guardians of the Whills.

420
00:30:21,612 --> 00:30:23,196
Protectors of the Kyber Temple.

421
00:30:24,073 --> 00:30:26,241
But there's nothing left to protect.

422
00:30:26,408 --> 00:30:28,910
So now they're just
causing trouble for everybody.

423
00:30:30,621 --> 00:30:32,622
You seem awfully tense all of a sudden.

424
00:30:32,790 --> 00:30:36,668
We have to hurry.
This town is ready to blow.

425
00:30:38,045 --> 00:30:39,712
<i>MALE IMPERIAL ANNOUNCER:
Citizens of the Empire...</i>

426
00:30:40,464 --> 00:30:44,551
<i>Imperial forces tirelessly fight
Saw Gerrera's reign of terror...</i>

427
00:30:44,718 --> 00:30:47,345
<i>over the people of this beloved city.</i>

428
00:30:47,513 --> 00:30:50,932
<i>Truth and justice
are the tools of the Empire.</i>

429
00:30:51,225 --> 00:30:52,725
(ANNOUNCEMENT
CONTINUES INDISTINCTLY)

430
00:30:55,896 --> 00:30:56,896
(SPEAKS ALIEN LANGUAGE)

431
00:31:03,445 --> 00:31:04,487
(SPEAKING ALIEN LANGUAGE)

432
00:31:08,284 --> 00:31:10,493
Tell me you have a backup plan.

433
00:31:15,040 --> 00:31:16,124
- (GUNFIRE)
- (ALL SCREAMING)

434
00:31:16,208 --> 00:31:16,874
<i>Incoming!</i>

435
00:31:18,043 --> 00:31:19,919
- (GUNFIRE)
- (INDISTINCT SHOUTING)

436
00:31:32,516 --> 00:31:34,767
Looks like we found Saw's rebels.

437
00:31:40,774 --> 00:31:41,649
<i>Up there!</i>

438
00:31:41,942 --> 00:31:43,443
(CHILD WAILING)

439
00:31:44,778 --> 00:31:45,445
Jyn, no!

440
00:31:53,537 --> 00:31:55,955
(WOMAN SHOUTS)

441
00:31:58,667 --> 00:31:59,584
<i>Hit the terrorist.</i>

442
00:32:00,502 --> 00:32:01,377
Get out of there!

443
00:32:06,133 --> 00:32:07,717
(SHOUTS)

444
00:32:18,395 --> 00:32:19,771
(MAN SCREAMS)

445
00:32:26,862 --> 00:32:28,488
(SHOUTING IN ALIEN LANGUAGE)

446
00:32:37,373 --> 00:32:39,040
Kyber... (SPEAKS ALIEN LANGUAGE)

447
00:32:43,337 --> 00:32:44,462
Come on!

448
00:32:46,090 --> 00:32:48,174
(GUNFIRE AND
SHOUTING CONTINUE)

449
00:33:04,525 --> 00:33:05,525
This way!

450
00:33:06,985 --> 00:33:08,236
Cassian!

451
00:33:11,115 --> 00:33:12,865
(BATON CLICKING)

452
00:33:15,160 --> 00:33:16,369
(JYN GRUNTING)

453
00:33:21,709 --> 00:33:23,251
(STORMTROOPER GROANS)

454
00:33:31,051 --> 00:33:32,802
Did you know that wasn't me?

455
00:33:33,595 --> 00:33:35,221
Yeah. Of course.

456
00:33:35,389 --> 00:33:37,306
I thought I told you to stay on the ship.

457
00:33:37,891 --> 00:33:40,309
You did. But I thought it was boring,

458
00:33:40,394 --> 00:33:41,394
and you were in trouble.

459
00:33:44,106 --> 00:33:45,732
There were a lot of explosions...

460
00:33:45,899 --> 00:33:47,483
- for two people blending in.
- STORMTROOPER: Freeze!

461
00:33:50,446 --> 00:33:51,446
You're right.

462
00:33:51,530 --> 00:33:53,239
I should just wait on the ship.

463
00:33:58,203 --> 00:34:00,288
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

464
00:34:05,544 --> 00:34:07,920
<i>STORMTROOPER:
Halt. Stop right there.</i>

465
00:34:10,716 --> 00:34:12,049
<i>Where are you taking these prisoners?</i>

466
00:34:13,594 --> 00:34:15,928
<i>- These are prisoners.
- Yes. Where are you taking them?</i>

467
00:34:16,096 --> 00:34:20,725
I am taking them
to imprison them in prison.

468
00:34:20,893 --> 00:34:22,477
- He's taking us to... (GROANS)
- Quiet!

469
00:34:23,395 --> 00:34:25,605
And there's a fresh one
if you mouth off again.

470
00:34:25,773 --> 00:34:27,023
<i>- We'll take them from here.
- That's okay.</i>

471
00:34:27,107 --> 00:34:28,357
If you could just point me
in the right direction,

472
00:34:28,442 --> 00:34:29,358
I can take them, I'm sure.

473
00:34:29,902 --> 00:34:31,486
- I've taken them this far.
- Hey, wait a second.

474
00:34:31,570 --> 00:34:32,653
<i>- Take them away.
- Wait.</i>

475
00:34:32,821 --> 00:34:34,197
You can't take them away.

476
00:34:34,364 --> 00:34:35,782
<i>You. Stay here.</i>

477
00:34:35,949 --> 00:34:37,158
<i>We need to check your diagnostics.</i>

478
00:34:37,785 --> 00:34:38,701
Diagnostics?

479
00:34:38,869 --> 00:34:40,703
I'm capable of running
my own diagnostics,

480
00:34:40,788 --> 00:34:41,788
thank you very much.

481
00:34:41,955 --> 00:34:43,581
CHIRRUT: Let them pass in peace.

482
00:34:49,421 --> 00:34:51,130
Let them pass in peace.

483
00:34:53,008 --> 00:34:54,801
The Force is with me.

484
00:34:54,968 --> 00:34:57,303
And I am with the Force.

485
00:34:57,471 --> 00:34:58,638
And I fear nothing.

486
00:34:58,722 --> 00:35:01,349
For all is as the Force wills it.

487
00:35:01,517 --> 00:35:03,434
<i>Hey, stop right there.</i>

488
00:35:03,602 --> 00:35:04,644
<i>He's blind.</i>

489
00:35:04,812 --> 00:35:06,187
<i>Is he deaf?</i>

490
00:35:06,355 --> 00:35:07,563
<i>I said stop right there!</i>

491
00:35:07,898 --> 00:35:09,065
(WEAPONS COCKING)

492
00:35:12,861 --> 00:35:14,570
(STORMTROOPERS GROANING)

493
00:35:22,079 --> 00:35:23,412
Is your foot all right?

494
00:35:24,331 --> 00:35:26,415
(GROANING CONTINUES)

495
00:35:47,354 --> 00:35:48,938
(JYN GASPS)

496
00:35:57,030 --> 00:35:58,531
You almost shot me.

497
00:35:58,699 --> 00:36:00,366
You're welcome.

498
00:36:04,788 --> 00:36:06,122
Clear of hostiles.

499
00:36:07,165 --> 00:36:09,125
- One hostile.
- He's with us.

500
00:36:09,251 --> 00:36:10,001
They're all right.

501
00:36:17,301 --> 00:36:18,551
Thanks.

502
00:36:20,012 --> 00:36:22,471
Cassian, I'm sorry about the slap.

503
00:36:23,098 --> 00:36:25,516
Go back to the ship. Wait for my call.

504
00:36:29,521 --> 00:36:30,438
Is he a Jedi?

505
00:36:30,606 --> 00:36:32,565
There are no Jedi here anymore.

506
00:36:32,733 --> 00:36:34,233
Only dreamers like this fool.

507
00:36:34,943 --> 00:36:36,235
The Force did protect me.

508
00:36:36,820 --> 00:36:37,820
I protected you.

509
00:36:37,988 --> 00:36:39,989
Can you get us to Saw Gerrera?

510
00:36:40,240 --> 00:36:42,575
(SHOUTING IN ALIEN LANGUAGE)

511
00:36:48,290 --> 00:36:51,083
Can't you see?
We are no friends of the Empire.

512
00:36:51,418 --> 00:36:53,920
(SPEAKING ALIEN LANGUAGE)

513
00:36:54,963 --> 00:36:56,464
Anyone who kills me or my friends

514
00:36:56,548 --> 00:36:58,382
will answer to Saw Gerrera.

515
00:37:01,261 --> 00:37:03,179
Because I'm the daughter of Galen Erso.

516
00:37:06,266 --> 00:37:07,767
(GRUNTING)

517
00:37:08,268 --> 00:37:11,103
Are you kidding me? I'm blind.

518
00:37:23,992 --> 00:37:25,618
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

519
00:37:51,853 --> 00:37:53,104
- (SHOUTING)
- (GROANS)

520
00:38:14,334 --> 00:38:17,628
(MUSIC AND ALIEN CHATTER)

521
00:38:48,368 --> 00:38:50,327
CHIRRUT: I'm one with the Force,
the Force is with me.

522
00:38:50,495 --> 00:38:51,871
I'm one with the Force,
the Force is with me.

523
00:38:52,038 --> 00:38:53,581
I'm one with the Force,
the Force is with me.

524
00:38:54,416 --> 00:38:55,416
You pray?

525
00:38:55,584 --> 00:38:57,835
I'm one with the Force,
the Force is with me.

526
00:38:58,003 --> 00:38:58,961
Really?

527
00:38:59,129 --> 00:39:00,588
I'm one with the Force,
the Force is with me.

528
00:39:01,214 --> 00:39:03,132
He's praying for the door to open.

529
00:39:04,050 --> 00:39:06,218
It bothers him because
he knows it's possible.

530
00:39:06,720 --> 00:39:08,345
(SNICKERING)

531
00:39:08,680 --> 00:39:12,600
Baze Malbus was once the most
devoted Guardian of us all.

532
00:39:13,268 --> 00:39:16,562
I'm beginning to think the Force and I
have different priorities.

533
00:39:16,730 --> 00:39:18,105
CHIRRUT: Relax, Captain.

534
00:39:18,315 --> 00:39:19,774
We've been in worse cages
than this one.

535
00:39:20,692 --> 00:39:21,817
This is the first for me.

536
00:39:23,695 --> 00:39:26,906
There is more than
one sort of prison, Captain.

537
00:39:27,032 --> 00:39:29,408
I sense that you carry yours
wherever you go.

538
00:39:30,702 --> 00:39:31,744
(BAZE SCOFFS)

539
00:39:35,540 --> 00:39:37,750
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

540
00:39:41,546 --> 00:39:42,922
(SPEAKING ALIEN LANGUAGE)

541
00:39:49,262 --> 00:39:50,262
SAW: Jyn.

542
00:39:52,015 --> 00:39:54,433
Is it really you?

543
00:39:55,227 --> 00:39:57,436
I can't believe it!

544
00:39:58,605 --> 00:40:00,314
Must be quite a surprise.

545
00:40:01,066 --> 00:40:04,610
Are we not still friends?

546
00:40:05,278 --> 00:40:06,362
The last time I saw you,

547
00:40:06,446 --> 00:40:07,613
you gave me a knife
and loaded blaster...

548
00:40:07,781 --> 00:40:10,366
and told me to wait
in a bunker till daylight.

549
00:40:10,492 --> 00:40:12,326
I knew you were safe.

550
00:40:12,452 --> 00:40:14,328
You left me behind.

551
00:40:14,538 --> 00:40:16,789
You were already
the best soldier in my cadre.

552
00:40:16,957 --> 00:40:18,833
- I was 16!
- I was protecting you!

553
00:40:19,000 --> 00:40:19,959
You dumped me!

554
00:40:20,126 --> 00:40:23,212
You were the daughter of
an Imperial science officer.

555
00:40:24,256 --> 00:40:26,423
People were starting to figure that out.

556
00:40:26,967 --> 00:40:30,386
People who wanted to
use you as a hostage.

557
00:40:33,139 --> 00:40:35,474
Not a day goes by...

558
00:40:36,059 --> 00:40:37,226
that I don't think of you.

559
00:40:42,440 --> 00:40:44,066
But today...

560
00:40:44,818 --> 00:40:46,652
of all days...

561
00:40:48,738 --> 00:40:50,322
(BREATH TREMBLING)

562
00:40:51,992 --> 00:40:52,992
It's a trap.

563
00:40:53,785 --> 00:40:55,494
Isn't it? (LAUGHS)

564
00:40:56,121 --> 00:40:57,037
What?

565
00:40:57,205 --> 00:40:58,497
The pilot.

566
00:40:58,707 --> 00:40:59,999
The message.

567
00:41:00,125 --> 00:41:01,166
All of it.

568
00:41:04,504 --> 00:41:05,921
(BREATHES DEEPLY)

569
00:41:14,347 --> 00:41:17,850
Did they send you?

570
00:41:20,854 --> 00:41:22,813
Did you come here...

571
00:41:23,732 --> 00:41:25,357
to kill me?

572
00:41:27,027 --> 00:41:28,861
There's not much of me left.

573
00:41:29,362 --> 00:41:31,363
The Alliance wants my father.

574
00:41:31,948 --> 00:41:34,366
They think he sent you
a message about a weapon.

575
00:41:34,534 --> 00:41:38,162
I guess they think by sending me,
you might actually help them out.

576
00:41:41,041 --> 00:41:44,043
So what is it that you want, Jyn?

577
00:41:46,922 --> 00:41:49,214
They wanted an introduction,
they've got it.

578
00:41:49,382 --> 00:41:50,633
I'm out now.

579
00:41:50,800 --> 00:41:52,635
Rest of you can do what you want.

580
00:41:53,386 --> 00:41:56,388
You care not about the cause?

581
00:41:56,556 --> 00:41:58,223
The cause?

582
00:41:58,391 --> 00:41:59,975
Seriously?

583
00:42:00,852 --> 00:42:02,478
The Alliance...

584
00:42:02,896 --> 00:42:04,146
the rebels, whatever it is

585
00:42:04,230 --> 00:42:05,564
you're calling yourself these days...

586
00:42:05,732 --> 00:42:07,900
all it's ever brought me is pain.

587
00:42:10,570 --> 00:42:12,738
You can stand to see the Imperial flag

588
00:42:12,822 --> 00:42:14,782
reign across the galaxy?

589
00:42:15,367 --> 00:42:17,743
It's not a problem if you don't look up.

590
00:42:21,247 --> 00:42:23,040
I have something to show you.

591
00:42:24,334 --> 00:42:25,334
Come.

592
00:42:30,256 --> 00:42:32,925
(DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING)

593
00:42:42,477 --> 00:42:44,520
The Emperor is awaiting my report.

594
00:42:44,688 --> 00:42:46,355
One would hope that he and Lord Vader

595
00:42:46,439 --> 00:42:47,815
might've been here
for such an occasion.

596
00:42:47,983 --> 00:42:49,274
And I thought it prudent to save you

597
00:42:49,359 --> 00:42:50,609
from any potential embarrassment.

598
00:42:50,777 --> 00:42:52,945
Your concern's hardly warranted.

599
00:42:53,113 --> 00:42:55,364
If saying it would only make it so.

600
00:42:57,701 --> 00:43:00,369
All Imperial forces
have been evacuated...

601
00:43:00,453 --> 00:43:03,622
and I stand ready to destroy
the entire moon.

602
00:43:03,790 --> 00:43:04,957
That won't be necessary.

603
00:43:05,041 --> 00:43:07,084
We need a statement, not a manifesto.

604
00:43:07,293 --> 00:43:09,837
The Holy City will be enough for today.

605
00:43:10,630 --> 00:43:12,089
Target Jedha City.

606
00:43:12,173 --> 00:43:14,174
Prepare single reactor ignition.

607
00:43:15,135 --> 00:43:16,385
(MECHANICAL WHIRRING)

608
00:43:19,347 --> 00:43:21,473
- PTERRO: Sir, we're in position...
- Fire!

609
00:43:22,058 --> 00:43:24,143
Commence primary ignition.

610
00:43:27,814 --> 00:43:29,231
Who's the one in the next cell?

611
00:43:29,983 --> 00:43:31,025
BAZE: What?

612
00:43:31,735 --> 00:43:33,152
Where?

613
00:43:37,782 --> 00:43:39,742
An Imperial pilot.

614
00:43:39,868 --> 00:43:40,951
- Pilot?
- BAZE: I'm gonna kill him!

615
00:43:41,119 --> 00:43:42,036
- No, no. No, wait!
- Come here!

616
00:43:42,245 --> 00:43:43,787
No!

617
00:43:43,913 --> 00:43:45,664
Back off! Back off!

618
00:43:48,168 --> 00:43:50,002
CASSIAN: Okay, okay.

619
00:43:50,754 --> 00:43:53,547
- Are you the pilot?
- (GROANING SOFTLY)

620
00:43:55,050 --> 00:43:59,053
Hey. Hey. Are you the pilot?
The shuttle pilot?

621
00:43:59,220 --> 00:44:00,512
Pilot?

622
00:44:00,638 --> 00:44:02,181
What's wrong with him?

623
00:44:04,726 --> 00:44:06,351
Galen Erso.

624
00:44:08,146 --> 00:44:09,563
You know that name?

625
00:44:11,107 --> 00:44:13,984
I brought the message. I'm the pilot.

626
00:44:16,404 --> 00:44:17,738
(CHUCKLES SLOWLY)

627
00:44:19,365 --> 00:44:20,949
I'm the pilot.

628
00:44:21,993 --> 00:44:23,368
I'm the pilot.

629
00:44:23,536 --> 00:44:25,204
Okay. Good.

630
00:44:25,997 --> 00:44:27,748
Now where is Galen Erso?

631
00:44:31,211 --> 00:44:32,211
ANNOUNCER: (OVER PA) Stand by.

632
00:44:38,218 --> 00:44:39,718
SAW: This is the message I was sent.

633
00:44:44,682 --> 00:44:47,101
<i>Saw, if you are watching this...</i>

634
00:44:47,268 --> 00:44:50,395
<i>then perhaps there's a chance
to save the Alliance.</i>

635
00:44:50,563 --> 00:44:52,689
<i>Perhaps there's a chance
to explain myself...</i>

636
00:44:52,816 --> 00:44:54,900
<i>and, though I don't dare
hope for too much...</i>

637
00:44:55,068 --> 00:44:57,569
<i>a chance for Jyn, if she's alive...</i>

638
00:44:57,737 --> 00:44:59,696
<i>if you can possibly find her...</i>

639
00:44:59,864 --> 00:45:04,618
<i>to let her know that my love
for her has never faded...</i>

640
00:45:05,120 --> 00:45:07,246
<i>and how desperately I've missed her.</i>

641
00:45:07,413 --> 00:45:08,580
(BEEPS)

642
00:45:11,000 --> 00:45:13,168
<i>Jyn, my Stardust...</i>

643
00:45:14,629 --> 00:45:17,172
<i>I can't imagine what you think of me.</i>

644
00:45:17,340 --> 00:45:21,093
<i>When I was taken,
I faced some bitter truths.</i>

645
00:45:21,261 --> 00:45:23,053
<i>I was told that soon enough</i>

646
00:45:23,138 --> 00:45:24,888
<i>Krennic would have you as well.</i>

647
00:45:25,014 --> 00:45:26,140
<i>As time went by...</i>

648
00:45:26,307 --> 00:45:28,267
<i>I knew that you were either dead...</i>

649
00:45:28,434 --> 00:45:30,769
<i>or so well hidden that
he would never find you.</i>

650
00:45:31,479 --> 00:45:34,273
<i>I knew if I had refused to work,
if I took my own life...</i>

651
00:45:34,440 --> 00:45:36,608
<i>it would only be a matter of time
before Krennic realized...</i>

652
00:45:36,776 --> 00:45:39,111
<i>he no longer needed me
to complete the project.</i>

653
00:45:39,195 --> 00:45:41,738
<i>So I did the one thing nobody expected.</i>

654
00:45:41,823 --> 00:45:42,865
<i>I lied.</i>

655
00:45:43,575 --> 00:45:45,450
<i>I learned to lie.</i>

656
00:45:45,618 --> 00:45:47,744
<i>I played the part of a beaten man</i>

657
00:45:47,829 --> 00:45:49,663
<i>resigned to the sanctuary of his work.</i>

658
00:45:49,873 --> 00:45:51,623
<i>I made myself indispensable...</i>

659
00:45:51,749 --> 00:45:55,878
<i>and all the while, I laid
the groundwork of my revenge.</i>

660
00:45:56,462 --> 00:45:58,422
<i>We call it the Death Star.</i>

661
00:45:58,590 --> 00:46:00,007
<i>There is no better name...</i>

662
00:46:00,133 --> 00:46:03,594
<i>and the day is coming soon
when it will be unleashed.</i>

663
00:46:03,761 --> 00:46:06,513
<i>I've placed a weakness
deep within the system...</i>

664
00:46:06,723 --> 00:46:09,224
<i>a flaw so small and powerful,
they will never find it.</i>

665
00:46:09,309 --> 00:46:10,475
<i>But, Jyn...</i>

666
00:46:11,019 --> 00:46:13,353
<i>Jyn, if you're listening, my beloved...</i>

667
00:46:14,522 --> 00:46:17,232
<i>so much of my life has been wasted.</i>

668
00:46:17,859 --> 00:46:21,278
<i>I try to think of you only
in the moments when I'm strong...</i>

669
00:46:21,446 --> 00:46:24,114
<i>because the pain of
not having you with me...</i>

670
00:46:24,282 --> 00:46:27,242
<i>your mother, our family.</i>

671
00:46:27,410 --> 00:46:29,453
<i>The pain of that loss
is so overwhelming...</i>

672
00:46:29,621 --> 00:46:31,622
<i>I risk failing even now.</i>

673
00:46:31,789 --> 00:46:34,249
<i>It's just so hard not to think of you.</i>

674
00:46:36,211 --> 00:46:38,003
<i>Think of where you are...</i>

675
00:46:39,380 --> 00:46:40,964
<i>my Stardust.</i>

676
00:46:42,342 --> 00:46:43,342
Saw...

677
00:46:43,593 --> 00:46:45,677
<i>the reactor module, that's the key.</i>

678
00:46:45,845 --> 00:46:47,679
<i>That's the place I've laid my trap.</i>

679
00:46:47,847 --> 00:46:50,098
<i>It's well hidden and unstable.</i>

680
00:46:50,683 --> 00:46:53,310
<i>One blast to any part of it
will destroy the entire station.</i>

681
00:46:54,854 --> 00:46:56,355
<i>You'll need the plans...</i>

682
00:46:56,522 --> 00:46:59,233
<i>the structural plans for the Death Star,
to find the reactor.</i>

683
00:47:00,026 --> 00:47:01,860
<i>I know there's a complete
engineering archive...</i>

684
00:47:02,028 --> 00:47:05,113
<i>in the data vault
at the Citadel Tower on Scarif.</i>

685
00:47:05,198 --> 00:47:07,699
<i>Any pressurized explosion
to the reactor module...</i>

686
00:47:07,867 --> 00:47:11,453
<i>will set off a chain reaction
that will destroy the entire station.</i>

687
00:47:13,164 --> 00:47:15,207
(RUMBLING)

688
00:47:23,216 --> 00:47:24,883
(SPEAKING IN ALIEN LANGUAGE)

689
00:47:28,221 --> 00:47:30,138
(RUMBLING CONTINUES)

690
00:47:38,564 --> 00:47:39,690
Go, go!

691
00:47:40,441 --> 00:47:42,401
(SHOUTING IN ALIEN LANGUAGE)

692
00:47:43,403 --> 00:47:44,987
K-2, K-2! Where are you?

693
00:47:45,571 --> 00:47:46,530
K-2SO: There you are.

694
00:47:46,739 --> 00:47:48,657
I'm standing by as you requested...

695
00:47:48,783 --> 00:47:50,993
although there's a problem
on the horizon.

696
00:47:51,703 --> 00:47:54,162
There's no horizon.

697
00:47:54,330 --> 00:47:56,999
Locate our position.
Bring that ship in here, now!

698
00:47:57,166 --> 00:47:58,417
Where are you going?

699
00:47:58,626 --> 00:48:00,043
I gotta find Jyn.

700
00:48:00,753 --> 00:48:01,795
Get the pilot, we need him!

701
00:48:01,963 --> 00:48:03,255
All right.

702
00:48:03,423 --> 00:48:04,923
I'll get the pilot.

703
00:48:12,557 --> 00:48:13,598
Pilot.

704
00:48:15,268 --> 00:48:16,018
No, no, no!

705
00:48:19,022 --> 00:48:20,272
Let's go.

706
00:48:20,440 --> 00:48:21,440
Jyn!

707
00:48:22,233 --> 00:48:23,233
Jyn!

708
00:48:27,655 --> 00:48:28,655
Hey.

709
00:48:29,949 --> 00:48:30,907
We gotta go.

710
00:48:31,951 --> 00:48:32,993
I know where your father is.

711
00:48:34,495 --> 00:48:36,163
Go with him, Jyn.

712
00:48:36,331 --> 00:48:37,331
You must go!

713
00:48:38,458 --> 00:48:39,374
Come with us.

714
00:48:39,542 --> 00:48:41,251
I will run no longer.

715
00:48:41,836 --> 00:48:43,587
- Come on.
- But you must save yourself.

716
00:48:44,172 --> 00:48:45,297
- Come on.
- Go!

717
00:48:45,465 --> 00:48:46,465
There's no time!

718
00:48:48,134 --> 00:48:49,885
SAW: Save the Rebellion!

719
00:48:50,762 --> 00:48:52,429
Save the dream.

720
00:48:53,973 --> 00:48:55,390
(RUMBLING CONTINUES)

721
00:48:57,852 --> 00:48:59,811
(SHOUTING IN ALIEN LANGUAGE)

722
00:49:12,825 --> 00:49:14,659
Oh, it's beautiful.

723
00:49:15,787 --> 00:49:17,579
(RUMBLING CONTINUES)

724
00:49:24,337 --> 00:49:25,379
Chirrut, let's go!

725
00:49:27,465 --> 00:49:28,507
Come on!

726
00:49:28,674 --> 00:49:30,425
Let's get out of here!

727
00:49:37,934 --> 00:49:39,434
(ENGINES ROARING)

728
00:49:46,025 --> 00:49:47,109
CASSIAN: Get us out of here!

729
00:49:47,276 --> 00:49:48,360
Punch it!

730
00:49:51,906 --> 00:49:53,198
I'm not very optimistic about our odds.

731
00:49:53,366 --> 00:49:54,366
Not now, K.

732
00:49:54,742 --> 00:49:56,284
(ENGINES ROARING)

733
00:49:57,787 --> 00:50:00,372
(THRILLING MUSIC PLAYING)

734
00:50:11,926 --> 00:50:13,468
(DECOMPRESSION HISS)

735
00:50:39,162 --> 00:50:40,287
(RUMBLING)

736
00:50:40,496 --> 00:50:41,371
Come on!

737
00:50:46,085 --> 00:50:47,252
Punch it.

738
00:50:47,420 --> 00:50:48,420
I haven't completed my calculations.

739
00:50:48,588 --> 00:50:50,672
I'll make them for you.

740
00:51:07,315 --> 00:51:09,566
(INDISTINCT CONVERSATIONS)

741
00:51:18,743 --> 00:51:21,870
I believe I owe you
an apology, Director Krennic.

742
00:51:22,038 --> 00:51:25,040
Your work exceeds all expectations.

743
00:51:28,169 --> 00:51:30,003
And you'll tell the Emperor as much?

744
00:51:30,171 --> 00:51:32,297
I will tell him that his patience
with your misadventures...

745
00:51:32,507 --> 00:51:33,840
has been rewarded with a weapon

746
00:51:33,925 --> 00:51:36,343
that will bring a swift end
to the Rebellion.

747
00:51:36,511 --> 00:51:38,553
And that that was only an inkling

748
00:51:38,638 --> 00:51:40,347
of its destructive potential.

749
00:51:40,515 --> 00:51:42,974
I will tell him that I will be
taking control over the weapon...

750
00:51:43,142 --> 00:51:46,686
I first spoke of years ago
effective immediately.

751
00:51:48,940 --> 00:51:50,065
(SCOFFS)

752
00:51:50,900 --> 00:51:53,860
We stand here amidst my achievement.

753
00:51:54,070 --> 00:51:55,570
Not yours!

754
00:51:55,780 --> 00:51:57,447
I'm afraid the recent security breaches...

755
00:51:57,615 --> 00:51:59,199
have laid bare your inadequacies

756
00:51:59,283 --> 00:52:01,034
as a military director.

757
00:52:01,244 --> 00:52:03,370
The breaches have been filled.

758
00:52:03,579 --> 00:52:06,164
Jedha has been silenced.

759
00:52:06,332 --> 00:52:07,999
You think this pilot acted alone?

760
00:52:08,167 --> 00:52:11,628
He was dispatched from
the installation on Eadu...

761
00:52:12,547 --> 00:52:14,923
Galen Erso's facility.

762
00:52:18,427 --> 00:52:20,095
Oh, we'll see about this.

763
00:52:24,850 --> 00:52:26,393
BASTEREN: A coded message
from Captain Andor, sir.

764
00:52:27,520 --> 00:52:28,645
"Weapon confirmed. "

765
00:52:29,188 --> 00:52:30,647
"Jedha destroyed. "

766
00:52:30,815 --> 00:52:34,484
"Mission target located
on Eadu, please advise. "

767
00:52:34,652 --> 00:52:35,485
Destroyed?

768
00:52:41,492 --> 00:52:42,659
Proceed.

769
00:52:43,661 --> 00:52:46,204
Tell him my orders still stand.

770
00:52:46,372 --> 00:52:48,373
Tell him to proceed with haste...

771
00:52:48,541 --> 00:52:49,958
and keep to the plan.

772
00:52:50,209 --> 00:52:52,586
We have no idea
what he's building for the Empire.

773
00:52:52,712 --> 00:52:56,131
We have to kill Galen Erso
while we have the chance.

774
00:52:56,340 --> 00:52:58,842
- (WHOOSHING)
- (INDISTINCT RADIO CHATTER)

775
00:53:06,350 --> 00:53:08,518
CHIRRUT: Baze, tell me.

776
00:53:10,396 --> 00:53:11,688
All of it?

777
00:53:12,398 --> 00:53:14,149
The whole city?

778
00:53:16,902 --> 00:53:17,944
Tell me.

779
00:53:18,112 --> 00:53:19,237
All of it.

780
00:53:26,912 --> 00:53:28,079
CASSIAN: Understood.

781
00:53:30,583 --> 00:53:32,500
(RADIO CONTROLS BEEP)

782
00:53:36,464 --> 00:53:37,922
Set course for Eadu.

783
00:53:38,090 --> 00:53:39,424
Setting course for Eadu.

784
00:53:39,592 --> 00:53:41,468
Is that where my father is?

785
00:53:42,511 --> 00:53:43,637
I think so.

786
00:53:43,804 --> 00:53:45,805
So you're Galen's daughter?

787
00:53:46,390 --> 00:53:47,265
You know him?

788
00:53:47,433 --> 00:53:50,101
I am Bodhi, the pilot.

789
00:53:50,269 --> 00:53:51,436
You brought the message.

790
00:53:51,520 --> 00:53:52,562
Yes.

791
00:53:52,730 --> 00:53:53,938
Your father...

792
00:53:54,106 --> 00:53:56,775
he said I could get right by myself.

793
00:53:57,360 --> 00:53:58,943
He said I could make it right...

794
00:53:59,111 --> 00:54:00,987
if I was brave enough...

795
00:54:01,906 --> 00:54:03,615
to listen to what was in my heart.

796
00:54:04,617 --> 00:54:06,451
Do something about it.

797
00:54:09,413 --> 00:54:10,538
Guess it was too late.

798
00:54:12,083 --> 00:54:13,458
It wasn't too late.

799
00:54:13,626 --> 00:54:15,919
Seems pretty late to me.

800
00:54:16,087 --> 00:54:17,504
JYN: No.

801
00:54:17,922 --> 00:54:20,423
We can beat the people who did this.

802
00:54:21,008 --> 00:54:23,426
My father's message, I've seen it.

803
00:54:25,012 --> 00:54:26,680
They call it the Death Star.

804
00:54:27,139 --> 00:54:28,306
But they have no idea...

805
00:54:28,474 --> 00:54:30,141
there's a way to defeat it.

806
00:54:30,309 --> 00:54:31,559
You're wrong about my father.

807
00:54:33,020 --> 00:54:33,770
He did build it.

808
00:54:33,979 --> 00:54:35,814
Because he knew
they'd do it without him.

809
00:54:36,440 --> 00:54:37,899
My father made a choice.

810
00:54:38,067 --> 00:54:40,443
He sacrificed himself for the Rebellion.

811
00:54:40,611 --> 00:54:41,986
He's rigged a trap inside it.

812
00:54:42,196 --> 00:54:44,489
That's why he sent you,
to bring that message.

813
00:54:44,699 --> 00:54:45,615
Where is it?

814
00:54:46,325 --> 00:54:47,701
Where's the message?

815
00:54:50,996 --> 00:54:52,163
It was a hologram.

816
00:54:53,499 --> 00:54:55,667
You have that message, right?

817
00:55:01,549 --> 00:55:04,008
Everything happened so fast.

818
00:55:04,802 --> 00:55:05,844
Did you see it?

819
00:55:09,014 --> 00:55:10,014
You don't believe me?

820
00:55:11,892 --> 00:55:14,352
I'm not the one you've got to convince.

821
00:55:14,520 --> 00:55:15,687
I believe her.

822
00:55:17,356 --> 00:55:18,732
That's good to know.

823
00:55:18,941 --> 00:55:20,066
What kind of trap?

824
00:55:21,527 --> 00:55:22,861
You said your father made a trap.

825
00:55:23,028 --> 00:55:25,155
The reactor.
He's placed a weakness there.

826
00:55:25,322 --> 00:55:26,239
He's been hiding it for years.

827
00:55:26,449 --> 00:55:28,408
He said if you can blow the reactor,

828
00:55:28,617 --> 00:55:30,368
the module,
the whole system goes down.

829
00:55:31,370 --> 00:55:33,037
You need to send word to the Alliance.

830
00:55:33,164 --> 00:55:33,955
I've done that.

831
00:55:34,081 --> 00:55:36,082
They have to know
there's a way to destroy this thing.

832
00:55:36,250 --> 00:55:38,042
They have to go to Scarif
to get the plans.

833
00:55:38,210 --> 00:55:39,794
I can't risk sending that.

834
00:55:39,879 --> 00:55:41,796
We're in the heart of Imperial territory.

835
00:55:43,007 --> 00:55:45,759
Then we'll find him and bring him back.

836
00:55:46,677 --> 00:55:48,136
And he can tell them himself.

837
00:55:53,476 --> 00:55:55,685
(MUSIC PLAYING)

838
00:56:06,071 --> 00:56:12,702
NAVIGATOR:
Course set for Eadu, sir.

839
00:56:26,801 --> 00:56:27,967
I'm one with the Force,
the Force is with me.

840
00:56:28,052 --> 00:56:29,260
I'm one with the Force,
the Force is with me.

841
00:56:29,345 --> 00:56:30,345
K-2SO: 20 degrees to the right.

842
00:56:32,223 --> 00:56:33,598
10 degrees up.

843
00:56:33,766 --> 00:56:34,933
Lower, lower, lower. Lower!

844
00:56:35,643 --> 00:56:36,810
Are you sure this is the way?

845
00:56:37,019 --> 00:56:38,144
BODHI: They have
landing trackers here.

846
00:56:38,354 --> 00:56:39,354
They have patrol squadrons.

847
00:56:39,480 --> 00:56:40,772
You've got to stay
in the canyon. Keep it low.

848
00:56:44,568 --> 00:56:45,610
(WARNING SYSTEMS BLARING)

849
00:56:45,945 --> 00:56:46,778
Watch your right!

850
00:56:51,158 --> 00:56:53,034
There's a 26*% chance of failure.

851
00:56:53,202 --> 00:56:54,118
How much farther?

852
00:56:54,286 --> 00:56:56,162
I don't know, I'm not sure.
I never really come this way.

853
00:56:56,330 --> 00:56:58,498
But we're close, we're close. I know that.

854
00:56:58,666 --> 00:56:59,916
Now, there's a 35% chance of failure.

855
00:57:00,000 --> 00:57:01,125
CASSIAN: I don't wanna know.
Thank you!

856
00:57:01,293 --> 00:57:02,252
I understand.

857
00:57:03,712 --> 00:57:04,963
Now! Put it down, now!

858
00:57:05,130 --> 00:57:06,256
The wind.

859
00:57:06,465 --> 00:57:08,091
If you keep going,
you'll be right over the shuttle depot.

860
00:57:08,968 --> 00:57:09,968
- Watch out!
- CASSIAN: K!

861
00:57:10,135 --> 00:57:11,177
(GRUNTING)

862
00:57:13,305 --> 00:57:14,389
Hold on tight!

863
00:57:14,515 --> 00:57:15,932
We're coming down hard!

864
00:57:16,225 --> 00:57:17,267
(ALARMS BLARING)

865
00:57:17,351 --> 00:57:18,560
(ENGINES ROARING)

866
00:57:28,320 --> 00:57:29,195
Try them again.

867
00:57:29,446 --> 00:57:31,322
I am, sir. We...

868
00:57:31,907 --> 00:57:33,074
The signal's gone dead.

869
00:57:35,494 --> 00:57:36,911
DRAVEN: Squadron up.

870
00:57:37,538 --> 00:57:38,913
Target Eadu.

871
00:57:47,172 --> 00:57:48,172
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

872
00:57:48,757 --> 00:57:50,174
How about now? Check stabilizers.

873
00:57:54,597 --> 00:57:56,097
Bodhi, where's the lab?

874
00:57:56,223 --> 00:57:57,181
The research facility?

875
00:57:57,349 --> 00:57:58,308
Yeah. Where is it?

876
00:57:58,434 --> 00:58:00,101
It's just over that ridge.

877
00:58:00,311 --> 00:58:02,520
That's a shuttle depot
straight ahead of us.

878
00:58:02,730 --> 00:58:04,355
- You are sure of that?
- Yes.

879
00:58:04,523 --> 00:58:05,773
We'll have to hope

880
00:58:05,858 --> 00:58:07,442
there's still an Imperial ship
left to steal.

881
00:58:08,193 --> 00:58:09,527
Here's what we're doing.

882
00:58:09,695 --> 00:58:12,572
Hopefully the storm keeps up
and keeps us hidden down here.

883
00:58:12,781 --> 00:58:14,616
Bodhi, you're coming with me.

884
00:58:14,783 --> 00:58:16,242
We'll go up the ridge and check it out.

885
00:58:16,452 --> 00:58:17,619
I'm coming with you.

886
00:58:17,786 --> 00:58:19,412
No, your father's message.

887
00:58:19,538 --> 00:58:21,706
We can't risk it. You're the messenger.

888
00:58:21,874 --> 00:58:23,374
That's ridiculous,
we all got the message.

889
00:58:23,459 --> 00:58:24,584
Everyone here knows it.

890
00:58:24,752 --> 00:58:25,835
(GUN CLICKS)

891
00:58:26,003 --> 00:58:27,170
"One blast to the reactor module

892
00:58:27,254 --> 00:58:29,005
"and the whole system goes down. "

893
00:58:29,173 --> 00:58:31,799
That's how you said it,
"The whole system goes down. "

894
00:58:31,967 --> 00:58:33,968
Get to work fixing our comms.

895
00:58:34,553 --> 00:58:37,931
All I want to do right now
is get a handle on what we're up against.

896
00:58:38,140 --> 00:58:40,934
So we're gonna go very small
and very careful up the rise...

897
00:58:41,101 --> 00:58:41,976
and see what's what.

898
00:58:42,895 --> 00:58:44,062
Let's get outta here.

899
00:58:46,982 --> 00:58:48,691
(THRILLING MUSIC PLAYING)

900
00:58:58,077 --> 00:58:59,869
Does he look like a killer?

901
00:59:00,079 --> 00:59:01,996
No. He has the face of a friend.

902
00:59:02,581 --> 00:59:03,915
Who are you talking about?

903
00:59:04,708 --> 00:59:06,501
Captain Andor.

904
00:59:06,669 --> 00:59:07,710
Why'd you ask that?

905
00:59:07,878 --> 00:59:09,170
What do you mean,
"Does he look like a killer?"

906
00:59:09,755 --> 00:59:11,255
The Force moves darkly

907
00:59:11,340 --> 00:59:13,257
near a creature that's about to kill.

908
00:59:15,594 --> 00:59:17,428
His weapon was
in the sniper configuration.

909
00:59:20,975 --> 00:59:22,600
(INDISTINCT ANNOUNCEMENT
ECHOING)

910
00:59:23,894 --> 00:59:26,062
No, no, no. We've got to go up.

911
00:59:26,230 --> 00:59:27,772
You can't see much from down there.

912
00:59:36,573 --> 00:59:37,740
(THRILLING MUSIC PLAYING)

913
00:59:38,409 --> 00:59:39,909
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

914
00:59:48,919 --> 00:59:51,963
(INDISTINCT ANNOUNCEMENT
CONTINUES)

915
00:59:54,425 --> 00:59:56,050
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

916
00:59:58,262 --> 00:59:59,345
(GRUNTS)

917
01:00:01,724 --> 01:00:02,724
This way.

918
01:00:03,642 --> 01:00:05,518
I'll be right behind you.

919
01:00:06,311 --> 01:00:07,520
Come on.

920
01:00:24,329 --> 01:00:25,913
Where are you going?

921
01:00:26,081 --> 01:00:27,999
I'm gonna follow Jyn.

922
01:00:28,167 --> 01:00:30,084
Her path is clear.

923
01:00:30,252 --> 01:00:31,836
Alone?

924
01:00:32,046 --> 01:00:33,337
Good luck!

925
01:00:33,505 --> 01:00:36,507
I don't need luck. I have you!

926
01:00:39,762 --> 01:00:41,220
(GROANS)

927
01:00:45,559 --> 01:00:47,101
What are they doing?

928
01:00:47,686 --> 01:00:50,188
If Cassian comes back,
we're leaving without them.

929
01:00:52,232 --> 01:00:54,067
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

930
01:00:57,029 --> 01:00:58,404
(THUNDER RUMBLES)

931
01:01:09,041 --> 01:01:10,708
You see Erso out there?

932
01:01:18,092 --> 01:01:19,634
BAZE: We've come too far.

933
01:01:20,052 --> 01:01:21,052
(GROANS)

934
01:01:22,763 --> 01:01:24,639
Patience, my friend.

935
01:01:24,807 --> 01:01:26,224
(PANTING)

936
01:01:34,900 --> 01:01:35,983
That's him.

937
01:01:36,151 --> 01:01:38,820
That's him. Galen, in the dark suit.

938
01:01:54,628 --> 01:01:57,338
Get back down there
and find us a ride outta here.

939
01:01:57,506 --> 01:01:59,590
- Well, what are you doing?
- You heard me.

940
01:01:59,758 --> 01:02:01,300
You said we came up here
just to have a look.

941
01:02:01,468 --> 01:02:03,636
I'm here, I'm looking. Go.

942
01:02:04,930 --> 01:02:06,013
Hurry!

943
01:02:06,181 --> 01:02:07,557
(DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING)

944
01:02:16,733 --> 01:02:18,276
KRENNIC: Excellent news, Galen.

945
01:02:18,443 --> 01:02:20,987
The battle station is complete.

946
01:02:21,613 --> 01:02:22,947
You must be very proud.

947
01:02:23,782 --> 01:02:25,491
Proud as I can be, Krennic.

948
01:02:25,701 --> 01:02:28,703
Gather your engineers.
I have an announcement.

949
01:02:30,706 --> 01:02:32,165
(PANTING)

950
01:02:41,466 --> 01:02:44,552
(INDISTINCT CONVERSATION)

951
01:02:44,928 --> 01:02:46,137
Is that all of them?

952
01:02:46,346 --> 01:02:47,638
Yes.

953
01:02:52,811 --> 01:02:55,188
Gentlemen, one of you...

954
01:02:55,772 --> 01:02:57,565
betrayed the Empire.

955
01:02:57,733 --> 01:02:59,066
(MEN GASPING AND EXCLAIMING)

956
01:02:59,151 --> 01:03:02,278
One of you has conspired with a pilot...

957
01:03:02,446 --> 01:03:05,406
to send messages to the Rebellion.

958
01:03:06,200 --> 01:03:08,492
And I urge that traitor...

959
01:03:08,660 --> 01:03:09,952
step forward.

960
01:03:15,167 --> 01:03:16,500
(INDISTINCT CONVERSATIONS
CONTINUE)

961
01:03:21,340 --> 01:03:22,340
(MECHANICAL VOICE SPEAKS)

962
01:03:24,009 --> 01:03:24,842
Very well...

963
01:03:25,010 --> 01:03:26,969
I'll consider it a group effort then.

964
01:03:27,596 --> 01:03:28,346
Ready!

965
01:03:28,513 --> 01:03:29,972
- No! No!
- Aim!

966
01:03:31,808 --> 01:03:32,934
And fire!

967
01:03:33,060 --> 01:03:34,560
Stop! Stop! Stop!

968
01:03:34,728 --> 01:03:35,645
Krennic, stop!

969
01:03:35,812 --> 01:03:37,021
It was me!

970
01:03:37,189 --> 01:03:39,065
It was me!

971
01:03:49,368 --> 01:03:50,868
They have nothing to do with it.

972
01:03:51,036 --> 01:03:52,411
Spare them.

973
01:04:03,882 --> 01:04:05,383
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

974
01:04:17,646 --> 01:04:18,354
Fire!

975
01:04:18,939 --> 01:04:20,398
(MEN GROANING)

976
01:04:21,400 --> 01:04:22,400
(GROANS)

977
01:04:30,742 --> 01:04:33,244
How do I know the weapon is complete?

978
01:04:33,412 --> 01:04:36,914
Let me share with you some details.

979
01:04:41,086 --> 01:04:42,503
(STORMTROOPER SCREAMS)

980
01:04:51,305 --> 01:04:52,054
K-2SO: Cassian.

981
01:04:52,931 --> 01:04:54,307
Cassian, can you hear me?

982
01:04:54,433 --> 01:04:55,850
<i>CASSIAN: I'm here.
You've got it working?</i>

983
01:04:56,018 --> 01:04:57,768
Affirmative, yes.
Although we have a problem.

984
01:04:57,936 --> 01:05:00,438
There's an Alliance squadron
approaching. Clear the area.

985
01:05:00,647 --> 01:05:02,815
No, no, no, no! Tell them to hold off!

986
01:05:02,983 --> 01:05:04,442
Jyn's on that platform.

987
01:05:07,404 --> 01:05:08,404
Jedha...

988
01:05:09,698 --> 01:05:12,658
Saw Gerrera. His band of fanatics...

989
01:05:12,826 --> 01:05:14,368
their Holy City...

990
01:05:14,536 --> 01:05:18,205
the last reminder of the Jedi, gone.

991
01:05:19,458 --> 01:05:20,875
You'll never win.

992
01:05:21,460 --> 01:05:24,253
Now where have I heard that before?

993
01:05:25,672 --> 01:05:27,131
<i>K-2SO: Relay from Captain Andor.</i>

994
01:05:27,716 --> 01:05:28,507
General.

995
01:05:28,717 --> 01:05:31,218
<i>Captain Andor requesting
a delay on squadron support.</i>

996
01:05:31,386 --> 01:05:33,929
<i>Alliance forces on site. Please confirm.</i>

997
01:05:34,097 --> 01:05:35,806
Get the squadron leader on.
Get him on now!

998
01:05:36,016 --> 01:05:37,224
They're already engaged, sir.

999
01:05:39,811 --> 01:05:41,687
(ALARM BLARING)

1000
01:05:44,566 --> 01:05:46,359
(DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING)

1001
01:05:57,162 --> 01:05:58,371
(MEN GROANING)

1002
01:06:01,666 --> 01:06:03,626
Jyn. No.

1003
01:06:04,669 --> 01:06:07,922
Return fire! To your stations!

1004
01:06:08,090 --> 01:06:10,174
Get our fighters in the air now!

1005
01:06:16,390 --> 01:06:17,431
Father!

1006
01:06:19,851 --> 01:06:21,894
(INDISTINCT SHOUTING)

1007
01:06:24,564 --> 01:06:26,065
(GROANING)

1008
01:06:30,862 --> 01:06:32,696
(SHOUTING CONTINUES)

1009
01:06:36,368 --> 01:06:38,619
<i>MALE IMPERIAL GUNNER:
Roger that. 3 through 7.</i>

1010
01:06:39,704 --> 01:06:41,205
(GUNS FIRING AND EXPLOSIONS)

1011
01:06:53,718 --> 01:06:55,886
GUARD: Fall back! Fall back!

1012
01:06:56,054 --> 01:06:59,056
Director, we need to evacuate.

1013
01:06:59,266 --> 01:07:01,058
(GROANING)

1014
01:07:05,647 --> 01:07:07,148
(GUNS FIRING)

1015
01:07:10,318 --> 01:07:11,652
(EXHALES)

1016
01:07:23,415 --> 01:07:24,957
(MAN SCREAMS)

1017
01:07:31,756 --> 01:07:33,340
(MECHANICAL VOICE SPEAKS)

1018
01:07:49,524 --> 01:07:51,066
(GROANING)

1019
01:07:52,652 --> 01:07:53,652
(GRUNTING)

1020
01:08:09,294 --> 01:08:11,545
Papa. Papa, it's me.

1021
01:08:15,133 --> 01:08:16,342
It's Jyn.

1022
01:08:17,135 --> 01:08:18,177
Jyn?

1023
01:08:20,388 --> 01:08:21,639
Stardust.

1024
01:08:22,516 --> 01:08:23,682
Papa.

1025
01:08:25,060 --> 01:08:26,644
I've seen your message.

1026
01:08:26,811 --> 01:08:28,771
The hologram, I've seen it.

1027
01:08:29,814 --> 01:08:31,857
It must be destroyed.

1028
01:08:32,025 --> 01:08:34,026
I know. I know.

1029
01:08:34,861 --> 01:08:35,861
We will.

1030
01:08:37,072 --> 01:08:38,322
Jyn.

1031
01:08:41,034 --> 01:08:42,034
Look at you.

1032
01:08:45,497 --> 01:08:47,748
I have so much to tell you.

1033
01:08:50,877 --> 01:08:52,002
(GALEN GROANS SLOWLY)

1034
01:08:58,510 --> 01:08:59,510
Papa.

1035
01:09:00,512 --> 01:09:01,470
No.

1036
01:09:01,638 --> 01:09:03,681
No! Papa.

1037
01:09:04,975 --> 01:09:06,308
Papa, come on!

1038
01:09:06,935 --> 01:09:08,102
<i>STORMTROOPER:
Over there! Take 'em down.</i>

1039
01:09:09,104 --> 01:09:11,480
Come on. Papa. Come on.

1040
01:09:13,817 --> 01:09:14,817
Jyn, we gotta go. Come on.

1041
01:09:14,943 --> 01:09:16,360
I can't leave him.

1042
01:09:16,528 --> 01:09:18,696
Listen to me, he's gone.

1043
01:09:18,905 --> 01:09:20,614
Nothing you can do. Come on.

1044
01:09:20,740 --> 01:09:22,116
- I can't leave him.
- Come on!

1045
01:09:22,242 --> 01:09:23,450
I can't.

1046
01:09:23,660 --> 01:09:24,660
Move!

1047
01:09:31,376 --> 01:09:32,876
<i>- This way, this way!
- CASSIAN: Down!</i>

1048
01:09:33,253 --> 01:09:35,087
(STORMTROOPERS YELLING)

1049
01:09:38,049 --> 01:09:39,258
Come on! Come on!

1050
01:09:55,900 --> 01:09:56,734
Well done.

1051
01:09:56,901 --> 01:09:59,069
You're a rebel now.

1052
01:09:59,446 --> 01:10:01,530
(DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING)

1053
01:10:06,077 --> 01:10:06,952
BODHI: Let's go! Let's go!

1054
01:10:07,078 --> 01:10:08,537
Come on, let's move!

1055
01:10:08,705 --> 01:10:10,581
Come on, let's get out of here!

1056
01:10:10,749 --> 01:10:12,166
Move, move, move!

1057
01:10:12,792 --> 01:10:15,252
Okay, K-2. Let's go!

1058
01:10:15,420 --> 01:10:16,545
Copy that.

1059
01:10:28,767 --> 01:10:30,059
(EXPLODING)

1060
01:10:34,439 --> 01:10:36,607
BODHI: lon thrusters low until
we've cleared the storm.

1061
01:10:36,775 --> 01:10:37,983
K-2SO: Understood.

1062
01:10:56,252 --> 01:10:57,628
You lied to me.

1063
01:10:58,630 --> 01:11:00,005
You're in shock.

1064
01:11:00,965 --> 01:11:02,800
You went up there to kill my father.

1065
01:11:04,135 --> 01:11:06,470
You don't know
what you're talking about.

1066
01:11:06,638 --> 01:11:08,013
Deny it.

1067
01:11:08,473 --> 01:11:11,975
You're in shock and looking
for some place to put it.

1068
01:11:12,143 --> 01:11:13,310
I've seen it before.

1069
01:11:13,478 --> 01:11:14,645
I bet you have.

1070
01:11:14,771 --> 01:11:15,646
They know.

1071
01:11:16,314 --> 01:11:18,982
You lied about why we came here
and you lied about why you went up alone.

1072
01:11:19,067 --> 01:11:20,734
(SIGHS)

1073
01:11:20,819 --> 01:11:23,028
I had every chance to pull the trigger...

1074
01:11:23,238 --> 01:11:24,822
but did I?

1075
01:11:27,867 --> 01:11:28,534
Did I?

1076
01:11:29,327 --> 01:11:30,494
You might as well have.

1077
01:11:31,496 --> 01:11:32,830
My father was living proof...

1078
01:11:32,997 --> 01:11:34,289
and you put him at risk.

1079
01:11:34,457 --> 01:11:36,792
Those were Alliance bombs
that killed him.

1080
01:11:37,001 --> 01:11:38,460
I had orders...

1081
01:11:38,628 --> 01:11:40,796
orders that I disobeyed.

1082
01:11:41,089 --> 01:11:42,464
But you wouldn't understand that.

1083
01:11:42,632 --> 01:11:43,716
Orders?

1084
01:11:43,842 --> 01:11:45,843
When you know they're wrong?

1085
01:11:47,637 --> 01:11:49,847
You might as well be a Stormtrooper.

1086
01:11:50,014 --> 01:11:51,306
What do you know?

1087
01:11:51,933 --> 01:11:53,726
We don't all have
the luxury of deciding...

1088
01:11:53,935 --> 01:11:56,186
when and where we want to
care about something.

1089
01:11:56,771 --> 01:11:58,939
Suddenly the Rebellion is real for you.

1090
01:11:59,482 --> 01:12:01,275
Some of us live it.

1091
01:12:02,068 --> 01:12:05,279
I've been in this fight
since I was 6 years old.

1092
01:12:07,866 --> 01:12:10,826
You're not the only one
who lost everything.

1093
01:12:12,036 --> 01:12:15,748
Some of us just decided
to do something about it.

1094
01:12:18,376 --> 01:12:20,711
You can't talk your way around this.

1095
01:12:24,466 --> 01:12:25,966
I don't have to.

1096
01:12:29,846 --> 01:12:31,305
Yavin 4.

1097
01:12:31,890 --> 01:12:35,225
Make sure they know
we're coming in with a stolen ship.

1098
01:12:38,730 --> 01:12:40,147
Anybody else?

1099
01:12:41,900 --> 01:12:43,192
(SIGHS)

1100
01:12:49,824 --> 01:12:51,408
(DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING)

1101
01:13:23,107 --> 01:13:24,399
(DOOR HISSING)

1102
01:13:37,455 --> 01:13:40,624
My lord, Director Krennic...

1103
01:13:40,792 --> 01:13:42,793
has arrived.

1104
01:13:43,628 --> 01:13:45,879
(MYSTERIOUS MUSIC PLAYING)

1105
01:13:51,886 --> 01:13:54,012
(DRAINING SOUND)

1106
01:14:18,830 --> 01:14:20,289
(RASPY BREATHING)

1107
01:14:20,373 --> 01:14:23,834
(DARTH VADER THEME PLAYING)

1108
01:14:43,187 --> 01:14:44,438
Director Krennic.

1109
01:14:45,982 --> 01:14:47,691
Lord Vader.

1110
01:14:48,693 --> 01:14:50,903
You seem unsettled.

1111
01:14:51,070 --> 01:14:52,279
No...

1112
01:14:52,447 --> 01:14:53,572
just pressed for time.

1113
01:14:53,740 --> 01:14:56,033
There's a great many things to attend to.

1114
01:14:56,200 --> 01:14:57,618
My apologies.

1115
01:14:57,785 --> 01:15:01,079
You do have
a great many things to explain.

1116
01:15:01,247 --> 01:15:03,624
I delivered the weapon
the Emperor requested.

1117
01:15:03,750 --> 01:15:05,584
I deserve an audience...

1118
01:15:05,710 --> 01:15:09,713
to make certain that
he understands its remarkable...

1119
01:15:11,174 --> 01:15:12,174
potential.

1120
01:15:12,342 --> 01:15:16,511
Its power to create problems
has certainly been confirmed.

1121
01:15:16,679 --> 01:15:18,597
A city destroyed...

1122
01:15:18,765 --> 01:15:21,725
an Imperial facility openly attacked.

1123
01:15:22,310 --> 01:15:25,145
It was Governor Tarkin
that suggested the test.

1124
01:15:26,314 --> 01:15:29,983
You were not summoned here
to grovel, Director Krennic.

1125
01:15:30,109 --> 01:15:31,109
No...

1126
01:15:31,194 --> 01:15:33,195
There is no Death Star.

1127
01:15:33,363 --> 01:15:34,571
The Senate has been informed...

1128
01:15:34,781 --> 01:15:38,033
that Jedha was destroyed
in a mining disaster.

1129
01:15:38,284 --> 01:15:39,242
Yes, my lord.

1130
01:15:39,410 --> 01:15:42,871
I expect you not to rest until
you can assure the Emperor...

1131
01:15:43,164 --> 01:15:45,499
that Galen Erso has not compromised

1132
01:15:45,583 --> 01:15:47,876
this weapon in any way.

1133
01:15:51,798 --> 01:15:54,257
So I'm still in command?

1134
01:15:57,220 --> 01:15:59,304
You'll speak to the Emperor about...

1135
01:15:59,472 --> 01:16:01,181
(CHOKING)

1136
01:16:12,443 --> 01:16:17,781
Be careful not to choke
on your aspirations, Director.

1137
01:16:18,241 --> 01:16:20,033
(GASPING)

1138
01:16:28,960 --> 01:16:31,086
PAMLO: We must scatter the fleet.

1139
01:16:31,879 --> 01:16:34,548
We have no recourse but to surrender.

1140
01:16:35,049 --> 01:16:37,300
BAIL: Are we really talking
about disbanding something...

1141
01:16:37,468 --> 01:16:39,469
that we've worked so hard to create?

1142
01:16:39,679 --> 01:16:41,221
We can't just give in!

1143
01:16:41,472 --> 01:16:43,306
We joined an alliance,
not a suicide pact.

1144
01:16:43,474 --> 01:16:44,808
We've only now managed
to gather our forces.

1145
01:16:45,309 --> 01:16:46,977
Gather our forces?

1146
01:16:47,145 --> 01:16:49,312
General Draven's already
blown up an Imperial base.

1147
01:16:49,480 --> 01:16:50,814
A decision needed to be made!

1148
01:16:51,149 --> 01:16:52,524
PAMLO: If it's war you want...

1149
01:16:52,734 --> 01:16:54,067
you'll fight alone.

1150
01:16:54,235 --> 01:16:56,069
If that's how it's going,
why have an alliance at all?

1151
01:16:56,237 --> 01:16:59,281
If she's telling the truth,
we need to act now!

1152
01:16:59,449 --> 01:17:00,782
Councilors, please.

1153
01:17:00,950 --> 01:17:01,950
It is simple.

1154
01:17:02,076 --> 01:17:04,578
The Empire has the means
of mass destruction...

1155
01:17:04,746 --> 01:17:05,829
the Rebellion does not.

1156
01:17:06,080 --> 01:17:07,789
A Death Star. This is nonsense.

1157
01:17:07,999 --> 01:17:09,499
What reason
would my father have to lie?

1158
01:17:09,709 --> 01:17:11,376
What benefit would it bring him?

1159
01:17:11,586 --> 01:17:13,378
To lure our forces into a final battle

1160
01:17:13,463 --> 01:17:14,838
to destroy us once and for all.

1161
01:17:15,590 --> 01:17:17,799
VASPAR: Risk everything?
Based on what?

1162
01:17:17,967 --> 01:17:19,176
The testimony of a criminal?

1163
01:17:19,385 --> 01:17:22,471
The dying words of her father,
an Imperial scientist?

1164
01:17:22,638 --> 01:17:24,431
JEBEL: But don't forget
the Imperial pilot.

1165
01:17:25,058 --> 01:17:27,142
My father gave his life so that
we may have a chance to defeat this.

1166
01:17:27,769 --> 01:17:28,727
So you've told us.

1167
01:17:28,895 --> 01:17:31,146
If the Empire has this kind of power,

1168
01:17:31,230 --> 01:17:32,522
what chance do we have?

1169
01:17:33,149 --> 01:17:35,025
What chance do we have?

1170
01:17:36,110 --> 01:17:37,694
The question is "what choice. "

1171
01:17:38,404 --> 01:17:39,529
Run, hide...

1172
01:17:39,697 --> 01:17:42,074
plead for mercy, scatter your forces.

1173
01:17:42,366 --> 01:17:45,035
You give way to an enemy this evil
with this much power...

1174
01:17:45,203 --> 01:17:48,121
and you condemn the galaxy
to an eternity of submission.

1175
01:17:48,289 --> 01:17:50,082
- The time to fight is now!
- ALL: Yes.

1176
01:17:50,249 --> 01:17:51,374
Every moment you waste

1177
01:17:51,459 --> 01:17:53,543
is another step closer
to the ashes of Jedha.

1178
01:17:54,712 --> 01:17:56,630
COUNCIL MEMBER 1:
What is she proposing?

1179
01:17:56,798 --> 01:17:57,798
COUNCIL MEMBER 2:
Just let the girl speak.

1180
01:17:58,049 --> 01:17:59,716
Send your best troops to Scarif.

1181
01:18:00,218 --> 01:18:01,885
(CROWD MURMURING)

1182
01:18:03,304 --> 01:18:04,721
Send the rebel fleet if you have to.

1183
01:18:05,473 --> 01:18:07,140
You need to capture
the Death Star plans

1184
01:18:07,308 --> 01:18:08,725
if there's any hope of destroying it.

1185
01:18:11,187 --> 01:18:12,312
(COUNCIL MUTTERING)

1186
01:18:13,606 --> 01:18:15,899
You're asking us to invade
an Imperial installation...

1187
01:18:16,067 --> 01:18:17,943
based on nothing but hope.

1188
01:18:20,071 --> 01:18:22,447
Rebellions are built on hope.

1189
01:18:24,617 --> 01:18:26,076
There is no hope.

1190
01:18:26,244 --> 01:18:27,869
I say we fight.

1191
01:18:27,995 --> 01:18:30,664
I say the Rebellion is finished!

1192
01:18:30,915 --> 01:18:31,957
(ALL MURMURING)

1193
01:18:35,294 --> 01:18:36,628
I'm sorry, Jyn.

1194
01:18:38,506 --> 01:18:40,799
Without the full support of the Council...

1195
01:18:42,927 --> 01:18:44,678
(SIGHS) the odds are too great.

1196
01:18:46,764 --> 01:18:47,764
(INDISTINCT WHISPERING)

1197
01:18:54,105 --> 01:18:55,564
(ALL MURMURING)

1198
01:19:04,490 --> 01:19:05,949
<i>REBEL ANNOUNCER:
General Syndulla,</i>

1199
01:19:06,033 --> 01:19:07,951
<i>please report to the briefing room.</i>

1200
01:19:09,620 --> 01:19:10,662
You don't look happy.

1201
01:19:11,289 --> 01:19:12,539
They prefer to surrender.

1202
01:19:12,707 --> 01:19:13,540
And you?

1203
01:19:14,041 --> 01:19:15,041
She wants to fight.

1204
01:19:15,209 --> 01:19:17,294
So do I. We all do.

1205
01:19:17,461 --> 01:19:19,504
The Force is strong.

1206
01:19:20,131 --> 01:19:22,299
I'm not sure four of us is quite enough.

1207
01:19:22,466 --> 01:19:23,800
How many do we need?

1208
01:19:23,968 --> 01:19:25,260
What are you talking about?

1209
01:19:29,807 --> 01:19:31,308
(INDISTINCT CONVERSATIONS)

1210
01:19:33,102 --> 01:19:35,478
They were never gonna believe you.

1211
01:19:35,646 --> 01:19:37,189
I appreciate the support.

1212
01:19:37,815 --> 01:19:38,982
But I do.

1213
01:19:41,527 --> 01:19:42,986
I believe you.

1214
01:19:48,159 --> 01:19:49,284
We'd like to volunteer.

1215
01:19:52,163 --> 01:19:53,830
Some of us...

1216
01:19:53,998 --> 01:19:55,749
Well, most of us...

1217
01:19:56,334 --> 01:19:59,586
we've all done terrible things
on behalf of the Rebellion.

1218
01:20:00,504 --> 01:20:01,838
Spies...

1219
01:20:02,506 --> 01:20:05,383
saboteurs, assassins.

1220
01:20:06,761 --> 01:20:10,013
Everything I did, I did for the Rebellion.

1221
01:20:11,557 --> 01:20:12,849
And every time I walked away...

1222
01:20:13,017 --> 01:20:15,393
from something I wanted to forget...

1223
01:20:16,520 --> 01:20:20,190
I told myself it was
for a cause that I believed in.

1224
01:20:21,359 --> 01:20:22,817
A cause that was worth it.

1225
01:20:24,403 --> 01:20:26,529
Without that, we're lost.

1226
01:20:27,698 --> 01:20:30,367
Everything we've done
would have been for nothing.

1227
01:20:33,746 --> 01:20:36,248
I couldn't face myself if I gave up now.

1228
01:20:39,877 --> 01:20:41,378
None of us could.

1229
01:20:46,425 --> 01:20:47,801
BODHI: It won't be comfortable.

1230
01:20:48,386 --> 01:20:50,845
It'd be a bit cramped, but we'd all fit.

1231
01:20:53,182 --> 01:20:54,599
We could go.

1232
01:20:56,560 --> 01:20:58,395
Okay. Gear up.

1233
01:20:59,021 --> 01:21:00,855
Grab anything that's not nailed down.

1234
01:21:00,940 --> 01:21:02,774
(REBELS TALKING INDISTINCTLY)

1235
01:21:02,858 --> 01:21:03,817
CASSIAN: Go, go, go!

1236
01:21:03,901 --> 01:21:04,985
K-2SO: Jyn.

1237
01:21:05,903 --> 01:21:07,988
I'll be there for you.

1238
01:21:09,907 --> 01:21:11,866
Cassian said I had to.

1239
01:21:17,748 --> 01:21:21,126
I'm not used to people sticking around
when things go bad.

1240
01:21:21,794 --> 01:21:23,295
Welcome home.

1241
01:21:25,715 --> 01:21:27,924
(INDISTINCT ANNOUNCEMENT
OVER PA)

1242
01:21:29,135 --> 01:21:31,428
- (CHEERFUL MUSIC PLAYING)
- (INDISTINCT CHATTER)

1243
01:21:47,737 --> 01:21:49,279
May the Force be with us.

1244
01:21:49,655 --> 01:21:51,239
(SCATTERED APPLAUSE,
LAUGHTER)

1245
01:21:55,494 --> 01:21:57,162
<i>DISPATCHER: Cargo shuttle,
read back please.</i>

1246
01:21:57,330 --> 01:21:58,330
<i>What's going on out there?</i>

1247
01:22:00,333 --> 01:22:01,458
<i>That ship's off-limits.</i>

1248
01:22:01,667 --> 01:22:04,419
<i>No one's supposed to be on board
until further instructions.</i>

1249
01:22:05,629 --> 01:22:06,963
Yes, yes, we are.

1250
01:22:07,131 --> 01:22:08,256
Affirmative.

1251
01:22:08,424 --> 01:22:09,841
<i>That's an impounded Imperial ship.</i>

1252
01:22:10,009 --> 01:22:12,218
<i>What's your call sign, pilot?</i>

1253
01:22:12,511 --> 01:22:14,471
- Um...
- We have to go.

1254
01:22:14,972 --> 01:22:16,014
It's, um...

1255
01:22:17,016 --> 01:22:18,308
Say something.

1256
01:22:18,809 --> 01:22:19,684
Come on.

1257
01:22:20,478 --> 01:22:21,394
Rogue.

1258
01:22:23,981 --> 01:22:25,190
Rogue One.

1259
01:22:25,316 --> 01:22:26,608
DISPATCHER: Rogue One?

1260
01:22:26,776 --> 01:22:29,194
<i>- There is no Rogue One!
- (BEEPING)</i>

1261
01:22:29,362 --> 01:22:30,653
Well, there is now.

1262
01:22:31,489 --> 01:22:33,448
Rogue One, pulling away.

1263
01:22:33,616 --> 01:22:35,116
Pulling away.

1264
01:22:50,091 --> 01:22:52,509
Despite what the others say,
war is inevitable.

1265
01:22:52,676 --> 01:22:53,676
Yes, I agree.

1266
01:22:53,844 --> 01:22:56,012
I must return to Alderaan
to inform my people

1267
01:22:56,138 --> 01:22:58,014
that there will be no peace.

1268
01:22:58,849 --> 01:23:00,850
We will need every advantage.

1269
01:23:01,936 --> 01:23:03,353
Your friend...

1270
01:23:04,355 --> 01:23:05,814
the Jedi.

1271
01:23:07,483 --> 01:23:09,526
He served me well
during the Clone Wars...

1272
01:23:09,693 --> 01:23:12,112
and has lived in hiding
since the Emperor's purge.

1273
01:23:12,279 --> 01:23:13,696
Yes, I will send for him.

1274
01:23:13,864 --> 01:23:16,116
You will need someone you can trust.

1275
01:23:18,119 --> 01:23:20,078
I would trust her with my life.

1276
01:23:20,663 --> 01:23:21,871
- Captain Antilles.
- Senator.

1277
01:23:22,039 --> 01:23:24,040
I have a mission for you, sir.

1278
01:23:25,876 --> 01:23:28,044
(SHIP WHOOSHING)

1279
01:23:34,051 --> 01:23:36,636
BODHI: Okay. We're coming in.

1280
01:23:37,221 --> 01:23:38,638
<i>There's a planet-wide defensive shield...</i>

1281
01:23:38,848 --> 01:23:40,390
with a single main entry gate.

1282
01:23:40,724 --> 01:23:42,142
This shuttle should be equipped with

1283
01:23:42,226 --> 01:23:44,394
an access code that allows us through.

1284
01:23:44,728 --> 01:23:46,896
Assuming the Empire hasn't
logged it as overdue.

1285
01:23:47,648 --> 01:23:49,274
And if they have?

1286
01:23:50,568 --> 01:23:51,734
Then they shut the gate.

1287
01:23:51,902 --> 01:23:53,236
And we're all annihilated

1288
01:23:53,320 --> 01:23:55,572
in the cold, dark vacuum of space.

1289
01:23:56,574 --> 01:23:57,907
Not me.

1290
01:23:59,368 --> 01:24:01,828
I can survive in space.

1291
01:24:02,538 --> 01:24:04,372
(DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING)

1292
01:24:12,339 --> 01:24:13,590
BODHI: Okay.

1293
01:24:13,757 --> 01:24:14,924
Here goes.

1294
01:24:19,346 --> 01:24:22,932
Cargo shuttle SW-0608
requesting a landing pad.

1295
01:24:25,686 --> 01:24:28,021
<i>GATE OFFICER:
Cargo shuttle SW-0608,</i>

1296
01:24:28,105 --> 01:24:29,981
<i>you're not listed on the arrival schedule.</i>

1297
01:24:30,149 --> 01:24:32,192
BODHI: Acknowledged, Gate Control.

1298
01:24:32,401 --> 01:24:35,069
<i>We were rerouted
from Eadu flight station.</i>

1299
01:24:35,237 --> 01:24:36,529
Transmitting clearance code now.

1300
01:24:36,739 --> 01:24:38,031
Transmitting.

1301
01:24:50,920 --> 01:24:53,296
<i>GATE OFFICER:
Cargo shuttle, SW-0608...</i>

1302
01:24:56,050 --> 01:24:57,800
<i>- you are cleared for entry.
- Yes!</i>

1303
01:24:58,093 --> 01:24:59,344
- (SIGHS)
- Impressive.

1304
01:24:59,553 --> 01:25:00,553
(CHUCKLES)

1305
01:25:04,642 --> 01:25:06,309
I'll tell the others.

1306
01:25:08,020 --> 01:25:09,145
Okay.

1307
01:25:13,442 --> 01:25:15,944
<i>SCARIF BASE ANNOUNCER: Tractor
beam test in bays 2 through 8.</i>

1308
01:25:16,111 --> 01:25:19,322
<i>Tractor beam test in bays 2 through 8.</i>

1309
01:25:27,039 --> 01:25:30,833
<i>GATE OFFICER: SW-0608,
cleared for Landing Pad 9.</i>

1310
01:25:30,960 --> 01:25:32,794
<i>Acknowledge, please.</i>

1311
01:25:33,003 --> 01:25:36,631
BODHI: SW-0608 proceeding
to LP 9 as instructed.

1312
01:25:37,341 --> 01:25:38,883
CASSIAN: Main building
down there, what is it?

1313
01:25:39,134 --> 01:25:40,551
BODHI: That's the Citadel Tower.

1314
01:25:40,719 --> 01:25:43,471
They keep all the Imperial
structural archives up there.

1315
01:25:43,681 --> 01:25:45,890
If the plans are anywhere,
they'll be there.

1316
01:25:46,016 --> 01:25:48,810
CASSIAN: And the dish
at the top, what's it for?

1317
01:25:49,520 --> 01:25:52,230
I guess it takes a lot of signal
to send those data files out.

1318
01:25:54,233 --> 01:25:56,859
Landing track, engaged.

1319
01:25:57,778 --> 01:25:58,820
Landing track locked.

1320
01:26:10,666 --> 01:26:11,749
We're landing.

1321
01:26:15,004 --> 01:26:16,462
We're coming in.

1322
01:26:21,343 --> 01:26:22,385
Saw Gerrera used to say...

1323
01:26:22,553 --> 01:26:27,181
one fighter with a sharp stick
and nothing left to lose can take the day.

1324
01:26:31,145 --> 01:26:33,021
They've no idea we're coming.

1325
01:26:33,856 --> 01:26:35,940
They've no reason to expect us.

1326
01:26:36,859 --> 01:26:38,151
If we can make it to the ground,

1327
01:26:38,235 --> 01:26:39,819
we'll take the next chance.

1328
01:26:40,612 --> 01:26:43,740
And the next. On and on until we win...

1329
01:26:46,160 --> 01:26:48,077
or the chances are spent.

1330
01:26:50,622 --> 01:26:53,041
The Death Star plans are down there.

1331
01:26:54,084 --> 01:26:57,420
Cassian, K-2, and I will find them.

1332
01:26:59,131 --> 01:27:00,757
We'll find a way to find them.

1333
01:27:02,551 --> 01:27:03,426
Melshi...

1334
01:27:04,595 --> 01:27:05,345
Pao...

1335
01:27:05,554 --> 01:27:06,596
Baze, Chirrut...

1336
01:27:06,805 --> 01:27:08,222
you'll take the main squad.

1337
01:27:08,390 --> 01:27:10,016
Move east and get wide of the ship.

1338
01:27:10,184 --> 01:27:12,393
Find a position between
here and the tower.

1339
01:27:13,312 --> 01:27:14,520
Once you get to the best spot...

1340
01:27:15,314 --> 01:27:16,439
light the place up.

1341
01:27:17,900 --> 01:27:19,859
Make 10 men feel like 100.

1342
01:27:20,194 --> 01:27:21,611
(MEN AGREEING)

1343
01:27:21,945 --> 01:27:24,113
And get those troopers away from us.

1344
01:27:24,656 --> 01:27:26,199
What should I do?

1345
01:27:26,367 --> 01:27:27,700
Keep the engine running.

1346
01:27:27,910 --> 01:27:30,536
You're our only way outta here.

1347
01:27:35,209 --> 01:27:37,335
(DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING)

1348
01:28:00,150 --> 01:28:03,778
<i>LANDING PAD OFFICER:
Cargo shuttle SW-0608...</i>

1349
01:28:03,987 --> 01:28:06,322
<i>be prepared to receive inspection team.</i>

1350
01:28:06,532 --> 01:28:07,532
Ready?

1351
01:28:21,839 --> 01:28:22,672
Hello.

1352
01:28:22,881 --> 01:28:23,881
Hey.

1353
01:28:23,966 --> 01:28:26,259
Oh, you're probably
looking for a manifest?

1354
01:28:26,427 --> 01:28:27,301
That would be helpful.

1355
01:28:29,221 --> 01:28:30,638
It's just down here.

1356
01:28:39,064 --> 01:28:40,106
IMPERIAL OFFICER: Director Krennic,

1357
01:28:40,190 --> 01:28:42,066
<i>we are entering the Scarif shield gate.</i>

1358
01:28:42,234 --> 01:28:44,902
<i>General Ramda has been
informed of your arrival.</i>

1359
01:28:45,487 --> 01:28:47,447
(THRILLING MUSIC PLAYING)

1360
01:29:09,219 --> 01:29:10,428
BAZE: Good luck...

1361
01:29:10,679 --> 01:29:12,221
little sister.

1362
01:29:18,228 --> 01:29:19,770
Go! Go now! You're clear!

1363
01:29:20,772 --> 01:29:23,232
MELSHI: All right, let's go!
Come on. Move, move, move.

1364
01:29:26,820 --> 01:29:30,406
<i>ANNOUNCER:
925-H to transport control.</i>

1365
01:29:30,574 --> 01:29:34,035
<i>925-H to transport control.</i>

1366
01:29:36,371 --> 01:29:38,414
(THRILLING MUSIC PLAYING)

1367
01:29:52,596 --> 01:29:53,763
I've got a bad feeling about...

1368
01:29:53,972 --> 01:29:54,972
- K!
- (WHISPERS) Quiet!

1369
01:29:55,140 --> 01:29:56,224
What?

1370
01:30:32,636 --> 01:30:33,970
We need a map.

1371
01:30:34,137 --> 01:30:36,681
Well, I'm sure there's one
just lying about.

1372
01:30:37,140 --> 01:30:39,350
You know what you have to do.

1373
01:30:48,944 --> 01:30:50,945
(INDISTINCT ANNOUNCEMENT
OVER PA)

1374
01:30:53,657 --> 01:30:55,992
(INDISTINCT CONVERSATIONS)

1375
01:31:09,756 --> 01:31:10,673
One per pad.

1376
01:31:10,841 --> 01:31:12,842
Pick your spot.
We wanna draw them out.

1377
01:31:13,510 --> 01:31:15,553
I'll call the timing. Go!

1378
01:31:18,140 --> 01:31:19,390
<i>STORMTROOPER 5:
Hey, did you hear the rumors?</i>

1379
01:31:19,558 --> 01:31:21,309
<i>STORMTROOPER 6: Yeah, the T-15s
have been marked obsolete.</i>

1380
01:31:21,476 --> 01:31:23,185
<i>STORMTROOPER 5: Oh boy,
it's about time for that.</i>

1381
01:31:24,104 --> 01:31:25,062
<i>Hey!</i>

1382
01:31:25,272 --> 01:31:26,564
(GROANING)

1383
01:31:29,860 --> 01:31:31,068
(CLEARS THROAT)

1384
01:31:32,738 --> 01:31:34,113
(GROANING)

1385
01:31:40,078 --> 01:31:41,370
(BEEPING)

1386
01:31:47,044 --> 01:31:48,377
<i>- What the...
- (GRUNTS)</i>

1387
01:31:54,009 --> 01:31:55,718
Director, what brings you to Scarif?

1388
01:31:55,802 --> 01:31:57,094
Galen Erso.

1389
01:31:57,262 --> 01:31:58,846
I want every dispatch,

1390
01:31:58,930 --> 01:32:01,432
every transmission he has ever sent...

1391
01:32:01,600 --> 01:32:02,933
called up for inspection.

1392
01:32:04,061 --> 01:32:05,061
RAMDA: All of them?

1393
01:32:05,854 --> 01:32:07,063
Yes, all of them.

1394
01:32:08,315 --> 01:32:09,482
Get started.

1395
01:32:11,318 --> 01:32:13,444
- (MUSIC PLAYING)
- (MOUSE DROID BEEPING)

1396
01:32:17,449 --> 01:32:18,699
(MECHANICAL WHIRRING)

1397
01:32:41,640 --> 01:32:42,640
K.

1398
01:32:43,183 --> 01:32:44,934
Our optimal route to the data vault

1399
01:32:45,018 --> 01:32:47,478
places only 89 Stormtroopers
in our path.

1400
01:32:47,646 --> 01:32:49,897
We will make it
no more than 33% of the way

1401
01:32:49,981 --> 01:32:51,107
before we are killed.

1402
01:32:57,698 --> 01:32:58,781
<i>Melshi, talk to me.</i>

1403
01:32:58,949 --> 01:33:01,033
Ready. Ready. Standing by.

1404
01:33:06,206 --> 01:33:07,248
Light it up.

1405
01:33:14,214 --> 01:33:15,214
(STORMTROOPER GROANS)

1406
01:33:15,340 --> 01:33:16,382
Come on.

1407
01:33:17,008 --> 01:33:18,008
(EXPLOSIONS ECHOING)

1408
01:33:31,064 --> 01:33:32,314
Are we blind?

1409
01:33:32,524 --> 01:33:33,983
Deploy the garrison!

1410
01:33:34,151 --> 01:33:35,234
Move!

1411
01:33:35,402 --> 01:33:36,694
(INDISTINCT SHOUTING)

1412
01:33:41,158 --> 01:33:43,534
(THRILLING MUSIC PLAYING)

1413
01:33:53,837 --> 01:33:54,670
Troopers!

1414
01:33:56,298 --> 01:33:57,465
Troopers! Troopers on the left.

1415
01:33:57,632 --> 01:33:59,133
Get in! Get in!

1416
01:34:06,016 --> 01:34:08,184
(ALARM BLARING)

1417
01:34:10,729 --> 01:34:12,605
(YELLING)

1418
01:34:16,902 --> 01:34:18,444
(MAN GROANS)

1419
01:34:24,326 --> 01:34:25,367
ROMODI: Sir, it's Scarif base.

1420
01:34:25,452 --> 01:34:26,994
They're reporting a Rebel incursion.

1421
01:34:27,078 --> 01:34:28,662
I want to speak with Director Krennic.

1422
01:34:28,872 --> 01:34:30,956
He's there, sir. On Scarif.

1423
01:34:31,875 --> 01:34:34,668
The original plans for this station
are kept there, are they not?

1424
01:34:34,836 --> 01:34:35,419
They are.

1425
01:34:36,546 --> 01:34:38,380
Prepare for the jump to hyperspace

1426
01:34:38,465 --> 01:34:40,424
and inform Lord Vader.

1427
01:34:48,016 --> 01:34:49,058
Can we help you?

1428
01:34:49,226 --> 01:34:50,351
That won't be necessary.

1429
01:34:50,936 --> 01:34:52,186
(GROANS)

1430
01:35:05,826 --> 01:35:07,409
Senator!

1431
01:35:09,120 --> 01:35:10,412
Senator!

1432
01:35:10,580 --> 01:35:11,747
Stop right there, Private.

1433
01:35:11,915 --> 01:35:13,249
Let him speak.

1434
01:35:14,251 --> 01:35:16,418
Intercepted Imperial
transmission, ma'am.

1435
01:35:16,586 --> 01:35:18,170
Rebels on Scarif.

1436
01:35:18,922 --> 01:35:20,631
I need to speak with Admiral Raddus.

1437
01:35:20,799 --> 01:35:22,675
He's returned to his ship.

1438
01:35:22,843 --> 01:35:24,510
He's going to fight.

1439
01:35:27,264 --> 01:35:29,348
(INDISTINCT YELLING)

1440
01:35:35,772 --> 01:35:36,772
No!

1441
01:35:39,442 --> 01:35:40,442
(GROANS)

1442
01:35:42,028 --> 01:35:43,904
<i>REBEL ANNOUNCER: Attention,
all flight personnel,</i>

1443
01:35:43,989 --> 01:35:45,573
<i>please report to
your commanders immediately.</i>

1444
01:35:46,992 --> 01:35:48,492
<i>All flight personnel,</i>

1445
01:35:48,618 --> 01:35:49,994
<i>please report to
your commanders immediately.</i>

1446
01:35:51,288 --> 01:35:53,289
<i>We have been redirected to Scarif.</i>

1447
01:35:54,040 --> 01:35:55,666
<i>Pilots, you'll be briefed</i>

1448
01:35:55,792 --> 01:35:57,668
<i>by your squadron leaders en route.</i>

1449
01:35:58,378 --> 01:36:00,296
<i>May the Force be with you.</i>

1450
01:36:00,964 --> 01:36:03,549
Scarif? They're going to Scarif?

1451
01:36:03,758 --> 01:36:06,260
Why does nobody
ever tell me anything, R2?

1452
01:36:06,344 --> 01:36:07,344
(R2-D2 BEEPING)

1453
01:36:09,639 --> 01:36:11,223
Move, move, move!

1454
01:36:13,059 --> 01:36:14,310
(SHOUTING)

1455
01:36:15,061 --> 01:36:17,605
Forward! Forward!

1456
01:36:17,772 --> 01:36:19,899
Keep drawing them out!

1457
01:36:22,068 --> 01:36:23,611
(GROANS)

1458
01:36:26,323 --> 01:36:27,323
OFFICER 1: Pad 12, report to ground.

1459
01:36:27,490 --> 01:36:28,657
<i>Coming in on our flank.
We need numbers.</i>

1460
01:36:28,825 --> 01:36:30,159
<i>OFFICER 2: Pad 14,
what's going on down there?</i>

1461
01:36:30,327 --> 01:36:33,037
<i>Status please.
All pads report in immediately.</i>

1462
01:36:33,204 --> 01:36:34,496
<i>OFFICER 3: Oh, no.
We have rebels everywhere!</i>

1463
01:36:34,581 --> 01:36:35,664
<i>We're taking fire!</i>

1464
01:36:35,832 --> 01:36:38,000
<i>Pad 12, Pad 14 request assistance.</i>

1465
01:36:38,877 --> 01:36:40,336
This is Pad 2. Pad 2.

1466
01:36:40,503 --> 01:36:42,463
I spot 40 rebels heading west on Pad 2.

1467
01:36:42,672 --> 01:36:44,840
Get on there. Tell him you're pinned
down by rebels on Pad 5.

1468
01:36:45,008 --> 01:36:47,718
<i>TONC: This is Pad 5!
We're being overrun! Help us!</i>

1469
01:36:48,053 --> 01:36:49,970
Pad 12, Pad 10, Pad 8, please confirm.

1470
01:36:50,055 --> 01:36:51,388
Confirm and report.

1471
01:36:52,349 --> 01:36:54,558
Get reinforcements down
to Pad 5 immediately!

1472
01:36:57,729 --> 01:36:59,521
CASSIAN: This is not working, K!

1473
01:37:00,523 --> 01:37:01,607
Right hand.

1474
01:37:11,701 --> 01:37:13,535
(MEN GROANING, YELLING)

1475
01:37:23,046 --> 01:37:24,046
Baze!

1476
01:37:25,674 --> 01:37:26,632
- Baze!
- What?

1477
01:37:26,716 --> 01:37:28,217
Run!

1478
01:37:30,720 --> 01:37:31,720
(GRUNTING)

1479
01:37:33,223 --> 01:37:35,349
<i>Karabast! AT-AT!</i>

1480
01:37:37,769 --> 01:37:38,435
Move!

1481
01:37:42,899 --> 01:37:44,316
(YELLING)

1482
01:37:50,365 --> 01:37:51,907
(DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYS)

1483
01:37:56,121 --> 01:37:58,372
This is Admiral Raddus
of the Rebel Alliance.

1484
01:37:59,082 --> 01:38:01,458
<i>All squadron leaders, report in.</i>

1485
01:38:01,626 --> 01:38:04,086
Admiral, this is Blue Leader standing by.

1486
01:38:04,254 --> 01:38:06,588
This is Gold Leader standing by.

1487
01:38:06,798 --> 01:38:09,049
This is Red Leader standing by.

1488
01:38:09,217 --> 01:38:11,427
Sir, those are rebel ships.

1489
01:38:11,928 --> 01:38:13,595
Get Admiral Gorin, immediately!

1490
01:38:14,597 --> 01:38:16,390
Director, the rebel fleet,

1491
01:38:16,474 --> 01:38:18,100
it's amassing outside the shield.

1492
01:38:20,937 --> 01:38:22,604
Lock down the base. Lock it down.

1493
01:38:22,731 --> 01:38:24,440
- And close the shield?
- Do it!

1494
01:38:24,941 --> 01:38:27,484
Red and Gold Squadrons,
attack formations.

1495
01:38:27,694 --> 01:38:29,111
<i>Defend the fleet.</i>

1496
01:38:29,279 --> 01:38:31,196
<i>Blue Squadron, get to the surface</i>

1497
01:38:31,281 --> 01:38:32,614
<i>before they close that gate.</i>

1498
01:38:32,741 --> 01:38:33,574
MERRICK: Copyyou, Admiral.

1499
01:38:33,700 --> 01:38:35,367
Blue Squadron, on me!

1500
01:38:35,535 --> 01:38:36,285
Copy, Blue Leader.

1501
01:38:36,411 --> 01:38:38,287
- Copy, Blue Leader.
- We won't have long.

1502
01:38:50,133 --> 01:38:52,968
Close the field aperture now! Close it!

1503
01:38:58,349 --> 01:38:59,016
Come on, come on, come on!

1504
01:39:00,060 --> 01:39:00,642
Pull up!

1505
01:39:01,644 --> 01:39:03,187
(SCREAMING)

1506
01:39:07,484 --> 01:39:08,984
(GUNS FIRING)

1507
01:39:13,656 --> 01:39:14,782
The rebel fleet has arrived.

1508
01:39:14,949 --> 01:39:15,949
What?

1509
01:39:16,117 --> 01:39:17,534
There's fighting on the beach.

1510
01:39:17,702 --> 01:39:19,620
They've locked down the base.

1511
01:39:19,704 --> 01:39:20,954
They've closed the shield gate.

1512
01:39:21,122 --> 01:39:22,414
What does that mean?

1513
01:39:25,001 --> 01:39:26,001
We're trapped?

1514
01:39:27,670 --> 01:39:30,422
We could transmit the plans
to the rebel fleet.

1515
01:39:30,632 --> 01:39:33,717
We'd have to get a signal up
to tell them it's coming.

1516
01:39:33,885 --> 01:39:35,010
It's the size of the data files.

1517
01:39:35,136 --> 01:39:36,220
That's the problem.

1518
01:39:36,387 --> 01:39:37,930
They'll never get through.

1519
01:39:38,515 --> 01:39:40,599
Someone has to
take that shield gate down.

1520
01:39:41,184 --> 01:39:43,143
Bodhi. Bodhi, can you hear me?

1521
01:39:43,394 --> 01:39:45,020
Bodhi, tell me you're out there.

1522
01:39:46,022 --> 01:39:47,064
Bodhi?

1523
01:39:47,232 --> 01:39:48,565
BODHI: I'm here.

1524
01:39:48,733 --> 01:39:49,817
<i>I was standing by.</i>

1525
01:39:49,984 --> 01:39:51,401
They've started fighting.
The base is on lockdown.

1526
01:39:51,569 --> 01:39:54,488
<i>I know. Listen to me.
The rebel fleet is up there.</i>

1527
01:39:54,656 --> 01:39:56,573
<i>You've gotta tell them to
blow a hole in the shield gate...</i>

1528
01:39:56,741 --> 01:39:58,867
<i>so we can transmit the plans.</i>

1529
01:39:59,035 --> 01:40:02,162
Wait. I can't. I'm not hooked
into the comms tower.

1530
01:40:02,330 --> 01:40:03,372
We're not tied in.

1531
01:40:03,540 --> 01:40:05,457
<i>It's the only way
we're getting them out of here.</i>

1532
01:40:05,625 --> 01:40:06,375
Find a way!

1533
01:40:07,210 --> 01:40:08,544
Cover our backs.

1534
01:40:10,797 --> 01:40:11,755
You'll need this.

1535
01:40:14,175 --> 01:40:15,175
You wanted one, right?

1536
01:40:17,595 --> 01:40:22,432
Your behavior, Jyn Erso,
is continually unexpected.

1537
01:40:23,226 --> 01:40:25,310
Jyn. Come on.

1538
01:40:29,399 --> 01:40:31,024
(YELLING CONTINUES)

1539
01:40:44,831 --> 01:40:46,081
<i>Sa'kalla!</i>

1540
01:40:46,166 --> 01:40:48,000
<i>Fire on my command.</i>

1541
01:40:48,751 --> 01:40:50,169
(SHOUTING CONTINUES)

1542
01:41:03,266 --> 01:41:03,891
Look!

1543
01:41:04,267 --> 01:41:05,559
(REBELS CHEERING)

1544
01:41:09,772 --> 01:41:11,440
(LAUGHING)

1545
01:41:15,278 --> 01:41:16,653
Get ready. We're gonna have
to go out there.

1546
01:41:19,657 --> 01:41:20,657
What are you doing?

1547
01:41:21,576 --> 01:41:23,452
They've closed the shield gate.

1548
01:41:23,620 --> 01:41:25,287
We're stuck here.

1549
01:41:25,455 --> 01:41:26,788
But the rebel fleet are pulling in.

1550
01:41:26,915 --> 01:41:29,041
We just have to get a signal
strong enough to get through to them...

1551
01:41:29,125 --> 01:41:31,418
and let them know
that we're trapped down here.

1552
01:41:31,586 --> 01:41:33,378
For that, we have to connect
to the communications tower.

1553
01:41:33,546 --> 01:41:35,714
Now, I can patch us in over here,
the landing pad.

1554
01:41:35,882 --> 01:41:37,090
But you have to get on the radio.

1555
01:41:37,258 --> 01:41:40,302
Get one of the guys out there
to find a master switch.

1556
01:41:40,470 --> 01:41:42,846
Get them to activate the connection
between us and that comms tower.

1557
01:41:43,097 --> 01:41:43,764
Okay?

1558
01:41:43,932 --> 01:41:45,224
Then go!

1559
01:41:48,603 --> 01:41:50,646
What's going on
down there, Lieutenant?

1560
01:41:50,813 --> 01:41:51,980
Unknown, sir.

1561
01:41:52,148 --> 01:41:53,232
We can't raise them.

1562
01:41:53,316 --> 01:41:54,483
All rebel frequencies are blocked.

1563
01:41:55,318 --> 01:41:57,861
Keep trying.
Engage those Star Destroyers

1564
01:41:58,029 --> 01:41:59,821
and let's start probing that shield!

1565
01:41:59,948 --> 01:42:01,156
Yes, sir!

1566
01:42:02,825 --> 01:42:04,326
REBEL PILOT: We're going in.

1567
01:42:10,124 --> 01:42:11,291
Stay with me.

1568
01:42:12,835 --> 01:42:14,753
(THRILLING MUSIC PLAYING)

1569
01:42:30,186 --> 01:42:32,020
(ALIEN SHRIEK)

1570
01:42:47,328 --> 01:42:50,038
<i>K-2SO: Schematic bank,
data tower two.</i>

1571
01:42:50,206 --> 01:42:51,248
How do I find that?

1572
01:42:51,416 --> 01:42:52,874
<i>Searching.</i>

1573
01:42:53,668 --> 01:42:54,835
I can locate the tape,

1574
01:42:54,919 --> 01:42:57,170
but you'll need to use
the handles for extraction.

1575
01:43:01,259 --> 01:43:03,677
What am I supposed to do with this?

1576
01:43:04,762 --> 01:43:06,346
Whoa!

1577
01:43:21,821 --> 01:43:22,738
Well, finally.

1578
01:43:22,947 --> 01:43:24,323
<i>Wait! Stop!</i>

1579
01:43:24,490 --> 01:43:27,367
The rebels, they went over there.

1580
01:43:27,535 --> 01:43:29,745
<i>CASSIAN: K, what's going on out there?</i>

1581
01:43:29,954 --> 01:43:30,746
There's one.

1582
01:43:31,831 --> 01:43:32,748
Ah, well.

1583
01:43:33,666 --> 01:43:35,959
(STORMTROOPERS GRUNTING)

1584
01:43:43,926 --> 01:43:44,843
Come on!

1585
01:43:52,518 --> 01:43:54,186
<i>Red Leader, this is Gold Leader.</i>

1586
01:43:54,312 --> 01:43:56,605
We're starting our attack run
on the shield gate.

1587
01:43:56,773 --> 01:43:58,982
<i>Keep it tight, and watch out
for those towers.</i>

1588
01:44:12,789 --> 01:44:15,957
More fighters. Form out at six-five.

1589
01:44:16,667 --> 01:44:19,544
Sir, enemy fighters coming in.

1590
01:44:26,010 --> 01:44:29,012
<i>TONC: Melshi! Melshi, come in.
Are you there?</i>

1591
01:44:29,180 --> 01:44:31,473
<i>Bodhi sent a signal from here.
He's patching us in.</i>

1592
01:44:31,641 --> 01:44:33,600
<i>But you guys have to open up
a line for the tower.</i>

1593
01:44:33,768 --> 01:44:35,310
How? Please advise.

1594
01:44:35,478 --> 01:44:37,729
There's a master switch
at the base of the comm tower.

1595
01:44:37,897 --> 01:44:40,357
Master switch? Describe.
What are we looking for?

1596
01:44:40,566 --> 01:44:43,652
What does it look like?
The master switch? Where is it?

1597
01:44:43,861 --> 01:44:46,405
<i>MERRICK: U-wings, reinforce
those troops on the beach.</i>

1598
01:44:46,614 --> 01:44:48,073
All fighters, on me.

1599
01:44:48,282 --> 01:44:49,783
We have to shield them from air attack.

1600
01:44:51,577 --> 01:44:53,787
Troop reinforcements. Here we go.

1601
01:44:56,707 --> 01:44:59,418
- For Jedha!
- (ALL YELLING)

1602
01:45:05,299 --> 01:45:07,342
We're having no effect on that shield.

1603
01:45:07,468 --> 01:45:09,219
How much more can that thing take?

1604
01:45:11,931 --> 01:45:14,182
Stick close, Red Five.
Where are you goin'?

1605
01:45:15,059 --> 01:45:16,977
<i>RED FIVE: They're all overme.
I'm trying to lose them!</i>

1606
01:45:18,354 --> 01:45:20,522
This is Red Five! I need help!

1607
01:45:26,946 --> 01:45:29,531
"Hyperspace tracking.
Navigational systems. "

1608
01:45:31,284 --> 01:45:32,284
Two screens down.

1609
01:45:32,368 --> 01:45:34,369
"Structural engineering. " Open that one.

1610
01:45:36,789 --> 01:45:37,664
<i>PILOT 1: I've got one on my tail!</i>

1611
01:45:38,749 --> 01:45:39,875
<i>PILOT 2: I'm on him!</i>

1612
01:45:44,964 --> 01:45:46,965
(YELLING CONTINUES)

1613
01:45:53,723 --> 01:45:58,185
Project code names: "Stellarsphere,
Mark Omega, Pax Aurora. "

1614
01:45:59,103 --> 01:46:00,103
(GRUNTS)

1615
01:46:09,989 --> 01:46:14,451
"War-Mantle, Cluster Prism,
Blacksaber. "

1616
01:46:15,161 --> 01:46:16,244
What?

1617
01:46:16,370 --> 01:46:17,662
"Stardust. "

1618
01:46:19,916 --> 01:46:20,916
That's it.

1619
01:46:21,083 --> 01:46:22,876
How do you know that?

1620
01:46:23,794 --> 01:46:25,128
I know because it's me.

1621
01:46:28,299 --> 01:46:30,800
<i>Hey, you! Identify yourself.</i>

1622
01:46:34,180 --> 01:46:35,764
- I can...
- (GROANS)

1623
01:46:36,557 --> 01:46:37,641
Incoming fire! Get cover!

1624
01:46:39,268 --> 01:46:41,269
(YELLING)

1625
01:46:45,983 --> 01:46:47,817
<i>CASSIAN: K, we need the file
for Stardust.</i>

1626
01:46:51,822 --> 01:46:52,697
Stardust.

1627
01:46:57,036 --> 01:46:57,786
That's it.

1628
01:47:19,642 --> 01:47:20,308
- (SHUTTING DOWN)
- K?

1629
01:47:21,018 --> 01:47:21,977
Climb.

1630
01:47:22,144 --> 01:47:23,144
<i>Climb.</i>

1631
01:47:23,980 --> 01:47:26,982
<i>You can still send the plans to the fleet.</i>

1632
01:47:27,942 --> 01:47:29,234
<i>If they open the shield gate...</i>

1633
01:47:29,402 --> 01:47:31,528
you can broadcast from the tower.

1634
01:47:32,738 --> 01:47:34,072
<i>Locking the vault door now.</i>

1635
01:47:34,198 --> 01:47:35,115
K?

1636
01:47:35,324 --> 01:47:36,199
K!

1637
01:47:36,367 --> 01:47:37,867
<i>- Goodbye.
- K!</i>

1638
01:47:55,177 --> 01:47:57,846
Sir, unauthorized access
at the data vault.

1639
01:47:59,015 --> 01:47:59,973
What?

1640
01:48:00,057 --> 01:48:01,683
It's just come in, sir.

1641
01:48:05,605 --> 01:48:07,272
Send my guard squadron into battle.

1642
01:48:07,356 --> 01:48:09,107
Two men with me, now.

1643
01:48:09,692 --> 01:48:12,360
Get that beach under control!

1644
01:48:13,696 --> 01:48:16,156
<i>CASSIAN: Bodhi, are you there?
Did you call the fleet?</i>

1645
01:48:16,782 --> 01:48:18,074
I can't get to the shuttle.

1646
01:48:19,285 --> 01:48:20,410
I can't plug in.

1647
01:48:21,078 --> 01:48:23,204
You have to. They have to hit that gate.

1648
01:48:23,372 --> 01:48:25,707
If the shield's open,
we can send the plans.

1649
01:48:28,002 --> 01:48:29,044
(DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING)

1650
01:48:29,629 --> 01:48:30,962
(SHOUTING CONTINUES)

1651
01:48:35,343 --> 01:48:37,052
(BODHI GROANING)

1652
01:48:56,197 --> 01:48:58,073
<i>PILOT: General, behind you!</i>

1653
01:48:58,324 --> 01:48:59,324
(BEEPING)

1654
01:49:01,994 --> 01:49:03,036
(YELLING)

1655
01:49:08,793 --> 01:49:10,418
(SHOUTING)

1656
01:49:11,420 --> 01:49:12,253
Step back.

1657
01:49:21,555 --> 01:49:23,098
We're going down!

1658
01:49:29,063 --> 01:49:30,021
Come on!

1659
01:49:39,573 --> 01:49:41,282
(THRILLING MUSIC PLAYING)

1660
01:49:46,080 --> 01:49:47,122
(INDISTINCT SHOUTING)

1661
01:50:02,263 --> 01:50:04,222
(PANTING)

1662
01:50:16,402 --> 01:50:17,986
(GRUNTING)

1663
01:50:26,871 --> 01:50:28,329
(GRUNTS)

1664
01:50:31,792 --> 01:50:33,001
Melshi, Melshi.

1665
01:50:33,169 --> 01:50:34,419
Come in, please.

1666
01:50:34,587 --> 01:50:35,837
<i>I'm tied in at my end.</i>

1667
01:50:36,005 --> 01:50:37,005
I just need an open line.

1668
01:50:37,673 --> 01:50:38,715
(COUGHS) Hang on.

1669
01:50:40,426 --> 01:50:41,468
The master switch.

1670
01:50:42,261 --> 01:50:44,012
It's over near that console.

1671
01:50:47,767 --> 01:50:48,516
I'm going!

1672
01:50:48,893 --> 01:50:50,018
(GROANING)

1673
01:50:58,360 --> 01:50:59,486
I've got it!

1674
01:51:01,781 --> 01:51:02,781
Careful!

1675
01:51:03,699 --> 01:51:04,491
You okay?

1676
01:51:14,043 --> 01:51:15,001
Jyn!

1677
01:51:19,924 --> 01:51:21,049
(GROANS)

1678
01:51:32,645 --> 01:51:35,313
I'm one with the Force,
the Force is with me.

1679
01:51:36,190 --> 01:51:37,398
I'm one with the Force,
the Force is with me.

1680
01:51:37,608 --> 01:51:38,274
Chirrut!

1681
01:51:43,823 --> 01:51:45,365
(MECHANICAL VOICE GRUNTING)

1682
01:51:48,369 --> 01:51:51,371
I'm one with the Force
and the Force is with me.

1683
01:51:51,539 --> 01:51:53,122
I'm one with the Force,
the Force is with me.

1684
01:51:53,374 --> 01:51:54,374
I'm one with the Force...

1685
01:51:54,542 --> 01:51:56,501
the Force is with me.
I'm one with the Force...

1686
01:51:56,669 --> 01:51:57,585
and the Force is with me.

1687
01:51:57,753 --> 01:52:00,088
I'm one with the Force,
and the Force is with me.

1688
01:52:00,256 --> 01:52:02,423
I'm one with the Force,
and the Force is with me.

1689
01:52:03,175 --> 01:52:04,926
Chirrut! Come back!

1690
01:52:05,135 --> 01:52:05,927
I'm one with the Force...

1691
01:52:14,603 --> 01:52:15,603
Yes!

1692
01:52:20,234 --> 01:52:21,401
Keep going! Keep going!

1693
01:52:23,737 --> 01:52:25,446
(SCREAMS)

1694
01:52:25,948 --> 01:52:27,782
Cassian!

1695
01:52:28,951 --> 01:52:30,034
(THUDS)

1696
01:52:37,126 --> 01:52:39,335
Chirrut! Come! Come with me!

1697
01:52:44,300 --> 01:52:45,592
Chirrut!

1698
01:52:45,926 --> 01:52:47,218
(PANTING)

1699
01:52:51,223 --> 01:52:52,140
Chirrut.

1700
01:52:52,725 --> 01:52:54,809
Don't go. Don't go.

1701
01:52:54,977 --> 01:52:56,477
I'm here, I'm here.

1702
01:52:57,313 --> 01:52:58,688
It's okay.

1703
01:52:59,356 --> 01:53:03,026
It's okay. Look for the Force.

1704
01:53:03,235 --> 01:53:04,527
Chirrut.

1705
01:53:04,737 --> 01:53:07,405
And you will always find me.

1706
01:53:08,532 --> 01:53:12,160
The Force is with me
and I'm one with the Force.

1707
01:53:13,537 --> 01:53:17,415
The Force is with me
and I'm one with the Force.

1708
01:53:17,958 --> 01:53:22,712
The Force is with me
and I'm one with the Force.

1709
01:53:29,386 --> 01:53:31,095
(DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING)

1710
01:53:36,352 --> 01:53:39,187
Deflector shields down to 50*%!
We're sustaining heavy damage!

1711
01:53:40,022 --> 01:53:41,314
There's no turning back now!

1712
01:53:41,482 --> 01:53:42,941
We have to press the attack!

1713
01:53:49,365 --> 01:53:50,365
GOLD LEADER: Hit that opening!

1714
01:53:50,532 --> 01:53:51,616
<i>GOLD NINE:
We see it, Gold Leader.</i>

1715
01:53:51,784 --> 01:53:53,368
lon torpedoes away!

1716
01:54:01,001 --> 01:54:02,126
(ENGINE SHUTTING DOWN)

1717
01:54:03,253 --> 01:54:04,212
IMPERIAL COMMANDER:
What's happening?

1718
01:54:04,380 --> 01:54:06,047
We've lost engine power, sir.

1719
01:54:09,176 --> 01:54:11,219
That Star Destroyer's disabled.

1720
01:54:12,888 --> 01:54:15,765
This is Rogue One calling
any Alliance ships that can hear me.

1721
01:54:17,893 --> 01:54:19,060
Is there anybody out there?
This is Rogue One.

1722
01:54:19,228 --> 01:54:20,228
<i>Come in, over!</i>

1723
01:54:20,562 --> 01:54:22,563
This is Admiral Raddus,
Rogue One. We hear you.

1724
01:54:24,066 --> 01:54:25,191
(LAUGHS)

1725
01:54:25,401 --> 01:54:26,859
We have the plans.

1726
01:54:27,736 --> 01:54:28,736
They found the Death Star plans.

1727
01:54:28,904 --> 01:54:30,863
They have to transmit them
from the communications tower.

1728
01:54:31,031 --> 01:54:32,115
You have to take down the shield gate.

1729
01:54:32,324 --> 01:54:34,367
<i>It's the only way
they're gonna get them through.</i>

1730
01:54:35,536 --> 01:54:38,579
Call up a Hammerhead corvette.
I have an idea.

1731
01:54:38,789 --> 01:54:40,248
<i>Stand by, Rogue One. We're on it.</i>

1732
01:54:40,457 --> 01:54:42,083
This is for you, Galen.

1733
01:54:42,710 --> 01:54:44,252
(YELLING CONTINUES)

1734
01:55:00,060 --> 01:55:01,811
(SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING)

1735
01:55:11,196 --> 01:55:14,449
The Force is with me,
and I'm one with the Force.

1736
01:55:16,160 --> 01:55:18,119
(WEAPONS FIRING)

1737
01:55:22,291 --> 01:55:24,000
(MECHANICAL VOICES GRUNTING)

1738
01:55:58,494 --> 01:56:00,203
(JYN GRUNTS)

1739
01:56:05,501 --> 01:56:07,210
Corvette Five, locked on target!

1740
01:56:08,796 --> 01:56:09,962
Prepare for impact.

1741
01:56:11,173 --> 01:56:12,507
(GUNS FIRING)

1742
01:56:19,139 --> 01:56:20,598
(GRUNTING)

1743
01:56:21,934 --> 01:56:23,726
Sublight thrusters, full power!

1744
01:56:32,820 --> 01:56:34,195
(WHOOSHING)

1745
01:56:38,826 --> 01:56:39,826
(GRUNTS)

1746
01:57:00,722 --> 01:57:02,807
<i>AUTOMATED VOICE:
Reset antenna alignment.</i>

1747
01:57:02,891 --> 01:57:04,225
(ALARMS BLARING)

1748
01:57:04,476 --> 01:57:05,893
<i>Reset antenna alignment.</i>

1749
01:57:07,104 --> 01:57:08,896
<i>Reset antenna alignment.</i>

1750
01:57:10,399 --> 01:57:12,233
<i>Reset antenna alignment.</i>

1751
01:57:12,901 --> 01:57:14,402
(THRILLING MUSIC PLAYING)

1752
01:57:36,216 --> 01:57:38,134
Reverse engines! Full power!

1753
01:57:45,767 --> 01:57:47,560
(MEN GROANING)

1754
01:57:59,531 --> 01:58:00,448
AUTOMATED VOICE: Antenna aligned.

1755
01:58:00,866 --> 01:58:02,158
<i>Ready to transmit.</i>

1756
01:58:10,626 --> 01:58:12,293
(GRUNTING)

1757
01:58:20,928 --> 01:58:22,553
(GASPS)

1758
01:58:23,305 --> 01:58:24,972
(STRAINING)

1759
01:58:36,985 --> 01:58:37,985
Who are you?

1760
01:58:40,322 --> 01:58:41,614
You know who I am.

1761
01:58:44,660 --> 01:58:45,826
I'm Jyn Erso.

1762
01:58:46,495 --> 01:58:48,371
Daughter of Galen and Lyra.

1763
01:58:48,997 --> 01:58:49,789
You've lost.

1764
01:58:50,666 --> 01:58:52,083
Oh, I have, have I?

1765
01:58:52,459 --> 01:58:53,918
My father's revenge.

1766
01:58:54,294 --> 01:58:55,586
He built a flaw in the Death Star.

1767
01:58:55,837 --> 01:58:57,672
He put a fuse in the middle
of your machine...

1768
01:58:57,839 --> 01:58:59,799
and I've just told the entire galaxy
how to light it.

1769
01:59:00,842 --> 01:59:03,261
The shield is up.

1770
01:59:03,428 --> 01:59:05,805
Your signal will never reach
the rebel base.

1771
01:59:05,973 --> 01:59:08,015
All your ships in the air
will be destroyed.

1772
01:59:08,183 --> 01:59:10,017
I lose nothing but time.

1773
01:59:10,435 --> 01:59:12,228
You, on the other hand...

1774
01:59:13,146 --> 01:59:15,439
die with the Rebellion.

1775
01:59:46,221 --> 01:59:47,305
AUTOMATED VOICE: Transmitting.

1776
01:59:49,683 --> 01:59:50,725
<i>Transmitting.</i>

1777
01:59:52,728 --> 01:59:55,771
Admiral, receiving
transmission from Scarif.

1778
02:00:03,864 --> 02:00:05,406
(GRUNTS)

1779
02:00:05,574 --> 02:00:07,241
Leave it, leave it!

1780
02:00:07,492 --> 02:00:08,576
That's it.

1781
02:00:09,786 --> 02:00:10,953
That's it.

1782
02:00:12,414 --> 02:00:13,414
Let's go.

1783
02:00:13,790 --> 02:00:15,458
<i>Transmission received.</i>

1784
02:00:15,625 --> 02:00:17,918
Admiral, we have the plans!

1785
02:00:18,253 --> 02:00:19,545
She did it!

1786
02:00:21,298 --> 02:00:24,216
Do you think anybody's listening?

1787
02:00:25,177 --> 02:00:26,344
I do.

1788
02:00:27,971 --> 02:00:29,847
Someone's out there.

1789
02:00:32,059 --> 02:00:34,101
Sir, we're detecting a massive object

1790
02:00:34,186 --> 02:00:36,395
emerging from hyperspace.

1791
02:00:42,235 --> 02:00:44,028
Sir, shall I begin targeting their fleet?

1792
02:00:44,196 --> 02:00:45,363
Lord Vader will handle the fleet.

1793
02:00:46,239 --> 02:00:49,742
Target the base at Scarif,
single reactor ignition.

1794
02:00:49,910 --> 02:00:51,118
Yes, sir.

1795
02:00:56,333 --> 02:00:57,333
Come on.

1796
02:01:21,149 --> 02:01:23,317
You may fire when ready.

1797
02:01:28,323 --> 02:01:29,865
<i>AUTOMATED VOICE: Commence
primary ignition.</i>

1798
02:01:52,055 --> 02:01:55,349
Rogue One, may the Force be with you.

1799
02:01:59,271 --> 02:02:02,523
<i>All ships prepare
for jump to hyperspace.</i>

1800
02:02:35,098 --> 02:02:37,183
Your father would have been
proud of you, Jyn.

1801
02:02:51,531 --> 02:02:53,741
IMPERIAL COMMANDER: The rebel
flagship is disabled, my lord...

1802
02:02:53,909 --> 02:02:56,118
but has received transmissions
from the surface.

1803
02:02:56,578 --> 02:02:58,829
Prepare a boarding party.

1804
02:02:59,080 --> 02:03:00,539
Yes, my lord.

1805
02:03:36,451 --> 02:03:37,159
Hurry!

1806
02:03:41,122 --> 02:03:43,165
Let's go! We gotta go, now!

1807
02:03:44,960 --> 02:03:46,627
Move! Move! Move!

1808
02:03:47,671 --> 02:03:48,963
Hurry. Let's go!

1809
02:03:49,130 --> 02:03:50,130
Let's go!

1810
02:03:50,257 --> 02:03:51,257
It's stuck!

1811
02:03:52,634 --> 02:03:53,634
Hey!

1812
02:03:54,010 --> 02:03:55,302
Hey! Help!

1813
02:03:56,555 --> 02:03:59,473
(ALARM SOUNDING)

1814
02:04:05,313 --> 02:04:07,147
(VADER BREATHING)

1815
02:04:12,195 --> 02:04:13,320
Open fire!

1816
02:04:19,327 --> 02:04:20,160
Help us!

1817
02:04:24,165 --> 02:04:24,748
It's jammed!

1818
02:04:26,209 --> 02:04:26,834
Pull it!

1819
02:04:32,716 --> 02:04:33,465
Pull it!

1820
02:04:37,596 --> 02:04:38,887
Here! Here!

1821
02:04:39,347 --> 02:04:40,639
Take it! Take it!

1822
02:04:48,523 --> 02:04:49,356
Launch!

1823
02:05:14,257 --> 02:05:17,009
(ALARM SOUNDING)

1824
02:05:17,177 --> 02:05:18,844
Make sure you secure the airlock.

1825
02:05:18,928 --> 02:05:20,721
And prepare the escape pods.

1826
02:05:25,060 --> 02:05:25,893
Your highness.

1827
02:05:26,811 --> 02:05:28,687
The transmission we received.

1828
02:05:29,731 --> 02:05:31,398
What is it they've sent us?

1829
02:05:33,068 --> 02:05:34,526
Hope.

1830
02:05:43,078 --> 02:05:45,371
(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)

